specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/plan.md:934:### ADR-003: Delegate anchor comparison to the template contract
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/plan.md:938:**Context**: A hand-rolled anchor set comparison would duplicate the contract and drift from the validator.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/plan.md:940:**Decision**: `check-example-drift.sh` calls `node runtime/cli/utils/template-structure.js compare <level> <doc> <example> anchors` and fails on any `missing_anchor` or `extra_anchor` line.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/plan.md:944:- The guard inherits the contract's dynamic ADR handling for `decision-record.md`.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/plan.md:949:### ADR-004: Examples satisfy required anchors and add no extra anchor
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/plan.md:953:**Context**: The contract marks some anchors optional, and an example may legitimately omit an optional section. Full equality would force optional sections into every example and would fight the dynamic ADR anchors.
specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/004-template-section-fill-guidance/plan.md:955:**Decision**: An example must carry every required anchor and no anchor outside the template's allowed set. Optional anchors may be absent.
