    12	---
    13	
    14	# Level Specifications - Complete Level 1-3+ Requirements
    15	
    16	Complete specifications for all documentation levels using the manifest-backed Level contract architecture where higher levels add value, not just length.
    17	
    18	---
    19	
    20	## 1. OVERVIEW
    21	
    22	### Template Architecture: Manifest-Backed Level Contracts
    23	
    24	Templates use a manifest-backed model where `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` selects rendered `*.md.tmpl` documents for each Level:
    25	
    26	```
    27	templates/
    28	├── spec-kit-docs.json       # Level contract and document membership
    29	├── spec.md.tmpl             # Requirements and scope
    30	├── plan.md.tmpl             # Technical approach
    31	├── tasks.md.tmpl            # Task breakdown
    32	├── acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl  # Closure criteria (Level 2+)
    33	├── decision-record.md.tmpl  # Architecture decisions
    34	├── implementation-summary.md.tmpl
    35	├── phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl
    36	├── handover.md.tmpl
    37	├── debug-delegation.md.tmpl
    38	├── resource-map.md.tmpl
    39	└── research.md.tmpl          # Optional research notes
    40	```
    41	
    42	### Template Paths - Quick Reference
    43	
    44	| Path | Purpose | When to Use |
    45	|------|---------|-------------|
    46	| `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` | Level contract and document matrix | **ALWAYS use this through `create.sh` for new specs** |
    47	| Level source contract | Source components | Reference only (understanding architecture) |
    48	| Level extension contract | Level additions | Reference only (understanding architecture) |
    49	
    50	> **IMPORTANT:** Always scaffold from the manifest-backed Level contract. `create.sh` selects and renders the correct template set for new spec folders.
    51	
    52	### Progressive Enhancement Model (Value-Based)
    53	
    54	```
    55	Level 1 (Core):         Essential what/why/how (~455 LOC)
    56	         ↓ +Verify
    57	Level 2 (Verification): +Quality gates, NFRs, edge cases (~875 LOC)
    58	         ↓ +Arch
    59	Level 3 (Full):         +Architecture decisions, ADRs, risk matrix (~1090 LOC)
    60	         ↓ +Govern
    61	Level 3+ (Extended):    +Enterprise governance, AI protocols (~1075 LOC)
    62	```
    63	
    64	### What Each Level ADDS (Value Scaling)
    65	
    66	| Level | Adds | New Content |
    67	|-------|------|-------------|
    68	| **L1 (Core)** | Essential what/why/how | Problem, scope, requirements, success criteria |
    69	| **L2 (+Verify)** | Quality gates | NFRs, edge cases, checklist, effort estimation |
    70	| **L3 (+Arch)** | Architecture decisions | Executive summary, ADRs, risk matrix, milestones |
    71	| **L3+ (+Govern)** | Enterprise governance | Approval workflow, compliance, AI protocols |
    72	
    73	**Key Points:**
    74	- LOC thresholds are **SOFT GUIDANCE** (not enforcement)
    75	- **Higher levels add VALUE** - not just more boilerplate
    76	- **Verification is script-assisted** - use `validate.sh`, `check-completion.sh`, and `check-placeholders.sh` where applicable
    77	- When in doubt, choose higher level
    78	
    79	**Note:** Single typo/whitespace fixes (<5 characters in one file) are exempt from spec folder requirements.
    80	
    81	---
    82	
    83	## 2. LEVEL 1: BASELINE DOCUMENTATION (LOC GUIDANCE: <100)
    84	
    85	### When to Use
    86	
    87	- **All features start here** - this is the minimum documentation for any work
    88	- Localized to one component or module
    89	- Includes trivial changes (typos, single-line fixes)
    90	- Clear, well-defined requirements
    91	- Low to moderate complexity
    92	
    93	### Required Files (Baseline)
    94	
    95	- `spec.md` - Requirements and user stories (scaffolded from `templates/core/spec.md.tmpl`)
    96	- `plan.md` - Technical implementation plan (rendered from `templates/core/plan.md.tmpl`)
    97	- `tasks.md` - Task breakdown by user story (rendered from `templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl`)
    98	- `implementation-summary.md` - Post-implementation documentation (rendered from `templates/core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl`)
    99	
   100	### Optional Files
   101	
   102	- `resource-map.md` - lean path catalog (cross-cutting, see §9)
   103	
   104	### Content Expectations
   105	
   106	**spec.md required sections:**
   107	- Problem statement or feature description
   108	- Proposed solution
   109	- Files to change
   110	- Testing approach
   111	- Success criteria
   112	
   113	**plan.md required sections:**
   114	- Implementation approach
   115	- File changes breakdown
   116	- Testing strategy
   117	- Dependencies
   118	
   119	**tasks.md required sections:**
   120	- Task breakdown by user story
   121	- Dependencies between tasks
   122	- Estimated effort per task
   123	
   124	**Enforcement:** Hard block if any required file missing
   125	
   126	### Example Scenarios
   127	
   128	**Good fits for Level 1:**
   129	- Fix "Error" → "Eror" typo
   130	- Update comment for clarity
   131	- Add email validation to contact form
   132	- Fix bug in calculation logic
   133	- Add loading spinner to form submission
   134	- Update error message formatting
   135	- Add new API endpoint (simple CRUD)
   136	- Refactor single component for clarity
   137	
   138	**Escalate to Level 2 if:**
   139	- Needs systematic QA validation
   140	- Affects multiple systems (not localized)
   141	- High risk (security, config cascades)
   142	- LOC estimate increases to 100+
   143	
   144	### Template Sources
   145	
   146	**Manifest templates (scaffolded by `create.sh`):**
   147	- `templates/core/spec.md.tmpl`
   148	- `templates/core/plan.md.tmpl`
   149	- `templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl`
   150	- `templates/core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl`
   151	
   152	**Core source (for reference):**
   153	- `templates/core/spec.md.tmpl`
   154	- `templates/core/plan.md.tmpl`
   155	- `templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl`
   156	- `templates/core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl`
   157	
   158	### Template Adaptation
   159	
   160	1. Fill metadata block (created date, status, level, estimated LOC)
   161	2. Replace `[PROBLEM]` with clear problem statement
   162	3. Replace `[SOLUTION]` with proposed approach
   163	4. List specific files to modify
   164	5. Define testing approach (unit tests, manual verification)
   165	6. State clear success criteria
   166	7. Fill plan.md with implementation steps
   167	8. Fill tasks.md with task breakdown
   168	9. Fill implementation-summary.md at end of implementation
   169	10. Remove all sample content and placeholders
   170	
   171	---
   172	
   173	## 3. LEVEL 2: VERIFICATION ADDED (LOC GUIDANCE: 100-499)
   174	
   175	### When to Use
   176	
   177	- Features needing systematic QA validation
   178	- Multiple files or components affected
   179	- Moderate complexity
   180	- High risk areas (security, config cascades)
   181	- Requires validation checklists
   182	
   183	### Required Files (Level 1 + checklist)
   184	
   185	- `spec.md` (from Level 1) - Requirements and user stories
   186	- `plan.md` (from Level 1) - Technical implementation plan
   187	- `tasks.md` (from Level 1) - Task breakdown by user story
   188	- `implementation-summary.md` (from Level 1) - Post-implementation documentation
   189	- `acceptance-criteria.md` (required at Level 2) - the criteria that decide whether the packet may close
   190	
   191	### Optional Files
   192	
   193	- `resource-map.md` - lean path catalog (cross-cutting, see §9)
   194	
   195	### Content Expectations
   196	
   197	**All Level 1 content expectations PLUS:**
   198	
   199	**acceptance-criteria.md required sections:**
   200	- Pre-implementation validation
   201	- Per-task verification
   202	- Integration testing steps
   203	- Security review checklist (if applicable)
   204	- Deployment verification
   205	
   206	**Enforcement:** Hard block if `acceptance-criteria.md` missing
   207	
   208	### Example Scenarios
   209	
   210	**Good fits for Level 2:**
   211	- Create reusable modal component with animations
   212	- Implement form validation framework
   213	- Add authentication flow
   214	- Migrate from library A to library B
   215	- Build file upload feature with progress tracking
   216	- Refactor state management approach
   217	- Config changes affecting multiple systems
   218	- Security-related changes
   219	
   220	**Escalate to Level 3 if:**
   221	- Requires architectural decisions to be documented
   222	- Discover >500 LOC during implementation
   223	- Complexity increases substantially
   224	- Need multiple developers for coordination
   225	- Architectural impact broader than anticipated
   226	
   227	### Template Sources
   228	
   229	**Manifest templates (scaffolded by `create.sh`):**
   230	- `templates/core/spec.md.tmpl`
   231	- `templates/core/plan.md.tmpl`
   232	- `templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl`
   233	- `templates/core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl`
   234	- `templates/addons/acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl`
   235	
   236	**Addendum source (+Verify):**
   237	- `templates/core/spec.md.tmpl`
   238	- `templates/core/plan.md.tmpl`
   239	- `templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl`
   240	
   241	### Template Adaptation
   242	
   243	**All Level 1 adaptations PLUS:**
   244	
   245	**acceptance-criteria.md:**
   246	1. Fill pre-implementation checks specific to feature
   247	2. Add implementation validation steps
   248	3. Define testing checklist items
   249	4. Include deployment verification steps
   250	5. Add security checks if applicable
   251	6. Remove all sample content
   252	
   253	### Level 2 Example: API Endpoint Feature
   254	
   255	**Scenario:** Adding a new REST API endpoint (~200 LOC)
   256	
   257	**Folder Structure:**
   258	```
   259	012-user-profile-api/
   260	├── spec.md                    # Requirements and scope
   261	├── plan.md                    # Technical approach
   262	├── tasks.md                   # Implementation tasks
   263	├── implementation-summary.md  # Post-implementation outcomes
   264	├── acceptance-criteria.md     # Closure criteria (Level 2+)
   265	├── description.json           # Generated packet metadata
   266	├── graph-metadata.json        # Generated graph metadata
   267	└── scratch/                   # Temporary files
   268	```
   269	
   270	**Checklist Example:**
   271	```markdown
   272	## Implementation Checklist
   273	
   274	### P0 - Blockers
   275	- [x] API endpoint responds to GET /users/:id [EVIDENCE: api.test.js:45-67]
   276	- [x] Authentication middleware applied [EVIDENCE: routes/users.js:12]
   277	
   278	### P1 - Required
   279	- [x] Input validation implemented [EVIDENCE: validators/user.js]
   280	- [x] Error responses follow API standard [EVIDENCE: manual test]
   281	
   282	### P2 - Nice to Have
   283	- [ ] Rate limiting (deferred to next sprint)
   284	```
