    13	
    14	# Template Style Guide - Formatting Standards
    15	
    16	Conventions and standards for system-spec-kit templates ensuring documentation consistency across all spec folders.
    17	
    18	---
    19	
    20	## 1. OVERVIEW
    21	
    22	### Core Principle
    23	
    24	Consistent templates enable predictable documentation structure, automated validation, and seamless context recovery across sessions.
    25	
    26	### When to Use This Guide
    27	
    28	- Creating new spec folder templates
    29	- Modifying existing template files
    30	- Validating template compliance
    31	- Understanding placeholder syntax
    32	- Troubleshooting validation failures
    33	
    34	### Template Inventory
    35	
    36	Current templates (user-facing only):
    37	
    38	| Level | Templates |
    39	|-------|-----------|
    40	| **Level 1** | spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, implementation-summary.md |
    41	| **Level 2, 3, 3+** | + acceptance-criteria.md; the higher levels add sections inside these files, not files |
    42	| **Lazy add-ons, every numbered level** | decision-record.md, before-after.md, timeline.md, roadmap.md, goal.md, resource-map.md, handover.md, debug-delegation.md, research/research.md |
    43	| **Written by a command or workflow** | handover.md, debug-delegation.md, research/research.md; phase parents omit the last two, and review and research packets omit goal.md as well |
    44	
    45	> **Flat, not cumulative:** the `lazyAddonDocs` list in `spec-kit-docs.json` is identical at Levels 1, 2, 3 and 3+. A level changes which sections a core template renders, never which add-ons exist. The packet-type rows are the only ones that narrow it, as the table says.
    46	
    47	---
    48	
    49	## 2. METADATA FORMAT
    50	
    51	### Standard Format
    52	
    53	Core spec templates use a markdown table for the METADATA section, as rendered by `spec.md.tmpl`:
    54	
    55	```markdown
    56	<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->
    57	## 1. METADATA
    58	
    59	| Field | Value |
    60	|-------|-------|
    61	| **Level** | 1 |
    62	| **Priority** | [P0/P1/P2] |
    63	| **Status** | [Draft/In Progress/Review/Complete] |
    64	| **Created** | [YYYY-MM-DD] |
    65	| **Branch** | `[###-feature-name]` |
    66	<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->
    67	```
    68	
    69	> **Note:** Bulleted-list metadata applies only to templates that actually use it (e.g. utility/ad-hoc docs). The core spec documents render the table format shown above.
    70	
    71	### Format Exceptions
    72	
    73	| Template | Format | Reason |
    74	|----------|--------|--------|
    75	| `debug-delegation.md` | Inline format | Auto-generated content structure |
    76	
    77	### Why Bulleted Lists
    78	
    79	- **Consistency** - Same format across all templates
    80	- **Readability** - Clear visual hierarchy
    81	- **Validation** - Easier to parse programmatically
    82	- **Flexibility** - Easy to add/remove fields
    83	
    84	---
    85	
    86	## 3. PLACEHOLDER SYNTAX
    87	
    88	### Placeholder Types
    89	
    90	| Format | Purpose | Example |
    91	|--------|---------|---------|
    92	| `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: description]` | User-provided values | `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: feature-name]` |
    93	| `[FORMAT: options]` | Constrained format | `[FORMAT: YYYY-MM-DD]` |
    94	| `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: question]` | Multi-choice questions | `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: (a) option (b) option]` |
    95	| `[OPTIONAL: description]` | Optional fields | `[OPTIONAL: link to spec.md]` |
    96	
    97	### Usage Guidelines
    98	
    99	**User-Provided Values:**
   100	```markdown
   101	- **Feature:** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: feature name]
   102	- **Owner:** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: team or person responsible]
   103	```
   104	
   105	**Constrained Formats:**
   106	```markdown
   107	- **Created:** [FORMAT: YYYY-MM-DD]
   108	- **Priority:** [FORMAT: P0 / P1 / P2]
   109	- **Status:** [FORMAT: Planning / In Progress / Complete]
   110	```
   111	
   112	**Clarification Needed:**
   113	```markdown
   114	- **Approach:** [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: (a) refactor existing (b) rewrite from scratch]
   115	```
   116	
   117	**Optional Fields:**
   118	```markdown
   119	- **Related Spec:** [OPTIONAL: link to related spec.md]
   120	- **Dependencies:** [OPTIONAL: list external dependencies]
   121	```
   122	
   123	---
   124	
   125	## 4. SECTION NUMBERING
   126	
   127	### Standard Format
   128	
   129	Use numbered sections with emoji and UPPERCASE:
   130	
   131	```markdown
   132	\## 1. SECTION NAME
   133	\## 2. ANOTHER SECTION
   134	\## 3. THIRD SECTION
   135	```
   136	
   137	### Emoji Usage
   138	
   139	Emojis are OPTIONAL in spec folder templates. When used:
   140	
   141	| Section Type | Emoji | Example |
   142	|--------------|-------|---------|
   143	| Overview/Summary | - | `## 1. OVERVIEW` |
   144	| Goals/Objectives | - | `## 2. GOALS` |
   145	| Implementation | - | `## 3. IMPLEMENTATION` |
   146	| Validation | - | `## 4. VALIDATION` |
   147	
   148	### Title Case Exception
   149	
   150	The following templates may use Title Case for improved readability:
   151	- `handover.md` - Session handover context
   152	- `implementation-summary.md` - Post-implementation summary
   153	
   154	---
   155	
   156	## 5. DATE FORMATS
   157	
   158	### Standard Format
   159	
   160	Always use ISO 8601 format: `YYYY-MM-DD`
   161	
   162	### Examples
   163	
   164	| Context | Format | Example |
   165	|---------|--------|---------|
   166	| Created date | `YYYY-MM-DD` | `2025-12-31` |
   167	| Updated date | `YYYY-MM-DD` | `2025-12-31` |
   168	| Placeholder | `[FORMAT: YYYY-MM-DD]` | User fills in |
   169	
   170	### Why ISO Format
   171	
   172	- **Unambiguous** - No confusion between MM/DD and DD/MM
   173	- **Sortable** - Alphabetical sort = chronological sort
   174	- **International** - Works across all locales
   175	
   176	---
   177	
   178	## 6. FILE NAMING
   179	
   180	### Naming Convention
   181	
   182	Templates use **kebab-case**: lowercase with hyphens.
   183	
   184	| Valid | Invalid |
   185	|-------------|-----------------|
   186	| `decision-record.md` | `DecisionRecord.md` |
   187	| `implementation-summary.md` | `implementation_summary.md` |
   188	| `spec.md` | `Spec.md` |
   189	
   190	### Template Markers
   191	
   192	All templates should include a source marker for validation and change tracking:
   193	
   194	```html
   195	<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: template-name | v1.0 -->
   196	```
   197	
   198	**Placement:** Near the top after YAML frontmatter and the H1 heading, as produced by `create.sh` (which moves the marker after the closing `---` of frontmatter).
   199	
   200	**Purpose:**
   201	- Enables automated validation
   202	- Tracks template version
   203	- Identifies template origin
   204	
   205	---
   206	
   207	## 7. FRONTMATTER REQUIREMENTS
   208	
   209	### When Required
   210	
   211	| Template Type | Frontmatter | Reason |
   212	|---------------|-------------|--------|
   213	| Continuity block (`_memory.continuity` in `implementation-summary.md`) | Required | Written by the continuity writer |
   214	| Spec folder files | Optional | Human-readable metadata |
   215	| Reference files | Required | Skill system indexing |
   216	
   217	### Continuity Block Frontmatter
   218	
   219	```yaml
   220	_memory:
   221	  continuity:
   222	    packet_pointer: [track/NNN-name]
   223	    last_updated_at: [ISO timestamp]
   224	    recent_action: [one sentence]
   225	    next_safe_action: [one sentence]
   226	```
   227	
   228	### Spec Folder File Frontmatter
   229	
   230	```yaml
   231	---
   232	title: [Document title]
   233	created: [YYYY-MM-DD]
   234	status: [Planning / In Progress / Complete]
   235	---
   236	```
   237	
   238	---
   239	
   240	## 8. VALIDATION RULES
   241	
   242	### Automated Checks
   243	
   244	The `validate.sh` script enforces these rules:
   245	
   246	| Rule | Check | Severity |
   247	|------|-------|----------|
   248	| Folder naming | `###-short-name` pattern | ERROR |
   249	| Required files | Level-appropriate files exist | ERROR |
   250	| Frontmatter syntax | Valid YAML | ERROR |
   251	| implementation-summary.md | Exists for completed specs | ERROR (Level 1+) |
   252	| Placeholder completion | No unfilled `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:]` | ERROR |
   253	
   254	### Manual Checks
   255	
   256	| Rule | Description |
   257	|------|-------------|
   258	| Metadata format | Bulleted list format used |
   259	| Date format | ISO 8601 (YYYY-MM-DD) |
   260	| Section numbering | Sequential, UPPERCASE |
   261	| File naming | kebab-case |
   262	
   263	---
   264	
   265	## 9. RELATED RESOURCES
   266	
   267	### Templates
   268	
   269	| Template | Location | Purpose |
   270	|----------|----------|---------|
   271	| All spec templates | `templates/` | Spec folder documentation |
   272	
   273	### Validation
   274	
   275	| Script | Purpose |
   276	|--------|---------|
   277	| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh` | Spec folder validation |
   278	| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-files.sh` | File existence checks |
   279	| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-folder-naming.sh` | Folder naming validation |
   280	| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-frontmatter.sh` | YAML frontmatter validation |
   281	
   282	### Related References
   283	
   284	- [validation-rules.md](../validation/validation-rules.md) - Complete validation rule documentation
   285	- [memory-system.md](../memory/memory-system.md) - Continuity artifact format and indexing
   286	- [folder-routing.md](../structure/folder-routing.md) - Spec folder organization
   287	
