   681	   ├── Full context passed
   682	   └── Parallel execution
   683	
   684	5. INTEGRATION
   685	   ├── Findings presented
   686	   ├── Fix proposed
   687	   └── User decides: Apply/Iterate/Manual
   688	```
   689	
   690	**Template Sections:**
   691	
   692	| Section | Purpose |
   693	|---------|---------|
   694	| Problem Summary | Error category, message, affected files |
   695	| Attempted Fixes | Document what was tried and why it failed |
   696	| Context for Specialist | Code snippets, docs, hypothesis |
   697	| Recommended Next Steps | Suggestions for the debugging agent |
   698	| Handoff Checklist | Verification that context is complete |
   699	
   700	**Model Selection Guidance:**
   701	
   702	| Scenario | Recommended Model |
   703	|----------|-------------------|
   704	| Common error patterns | Claude |
   705	| Type errors, syntax issues | Claude |
   706	| Architectural problems | Claude |
   707	| Complex state management | Claude |
   708	| Logic puzzles, algorithms | OpenCode |
   709	| Large codebase context | Claude |
   710	
   711	**Example Usage:**
   712	
   713	```bash
   714	# Manual trigger
   715	Task tool -> @debug for specs/007-feature/
   716	
   717	# Auto-suggested after repeated failures
   718	💡 Debug Delegation Suggested - Dispatch `@debug` via the Task tool
   719	```
   720	
   721	**Integration with SpecKit:**
   722	- Saved to spec folder root for reference
   723	- Found in future sessions by `/speckit:resume` walking the packet, or by a ripgrep sweep over the specs tree
   724	- Documents debugging history for the feature
