   726	---
   727	
   728	## 7. QUALITY STANDARDS
   729	
   730	### Adherence Rules
   731	
   732	**Non-negotiable:**
   733	
   734	1. **Always scaffold or render from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/`** - Never freehand
   735	2. **Preserve numbering and emojis** - Maintain visual scanning pattern
   736	3. **Fill every placeholder** - Replace `[PLACEHOLDER]` with actual content
   737	4. **Remove instructional comments** - Delete `<!-- SAMPLE -->` blocks
   738	5. **Use the canonical required filename** - `decision-record.md` (topic-specific ADR files are supplemental)
   739	6. **Keep sections relevant** - State "N/A" instead of deleting sections
   740	7. **Link sibling documents** - Cross-reference spec.md ↔ plan.md ↔ tasks.md
   741	8. **Document level changes** - Use `upgrade-level.sh` for level upgrades (recommended), then auto-populate placeholder content. Note changes in changelog
   742	9. **Keep history immutable** - Append to history, don't rewrite
   743	10. **Validate before coding** - Complete pre-implementation checklist first
   744	11. **Apply ToC policy consistently** - Only `research/research.md` may include a Table of Contents section; keep standard spec artifacts ToC-free
   745	
   746	### Pre-Delivery Checklist
   747	
   748	Before presenting documentation to user, verify:
   749	
   750	- [ ] All templates copied from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/` (not created from scratch)
   751	- [ ] All placeholders replaced (`[PLACEHOLDER]`, `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: ...]`)
   752	- [ ] All sample content removed (`<!-- SAMPLE CONTENT -->`)
   753	- [ ] Template footer deleted
   754	- [ ] Metadata block filled correctly
   755	- [ ] All sections filled with actual content (or marked "N/A")
   756	- [ ] Cross-references to sibling documents working
   757	- [ ] Numbering and emojis preserved
   758	- [ ] Structure matches template
   759	- [ ] Descriptive filenames used (for decision records)
   760	- [ ] No ToC heading in non-research spec artifacts (`spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `decision-record.md`, `implementation-summary.md`, `handover.md`, `debug-delegation.md`, `resource-map.md`)
   761	
   762	**If ANY unchecked → Fix before presenting to user**
   763	
   764	---
   765	
   766	### Script-Assisted Level Upgrades
   767	
   768	When scope grows during implementation and a level upgrade is needed, use `upgrade-level.sh` instead of manually copying templates:
   769	
   770	```bash
   771	# Upgrade spec folder to a higher level (auto-detects current level)
   772	bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-level.sh specs/042-feature/ --to 2
   773	
   774	# Preview changes without modifying files
   775	bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-level.sh specs/042-feature/ --to 3 --dry-run
   776	```
   777	
   778	The script handles structural changes (new files, addendum injection, backups). After it runs, the AI agent **must** auto-populate all `[placeholder]` text in newly injected sections by reading existing spec context and deriving appropriate content.
   779	
   780	Verify placeholder cleanup before completion:
   781	
   782	```bash
   783	.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-placeholders.sh specs/042-feature/
   784	```
   785	
   786	For manual upgrades (fallback), render the required manifest template for the target level and adapt it following the standard adaptation process above.
   787	
   788	---
   789	
   790	## 8. COMMON MISTAKES
   791	
   792	### Mistake 1: Creating from Scratch
   793	
   794	**Wrong:**
   795	```bash
   796	echo "# Spec" > specs/042-feature/spec.md
   797	```
   798	
   799	**Right:**
   800	```bash
   801	bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh --level 1 --path specs/042-feature --name feature-name
   802	```
   803	
   804	**Why wrong:** Loses structure, misses sections, inconsistent format
   805	
   806	---
   807	
   808	### Mistake 2: Leaving Placeholders
   809	
   810	**Wrong:**
   811	```markdown
   812	## Problem
   813	
   814	[PLACEHOLDER: Describe the problem]
   815	```
   816	
   817	**Right:**
   818	```markdown
   819	## Problem
   820	
   821	The form submission button doesn't show loading state, causing duplicate submissions.
   822	```
   823	
   824	**Why wrong:** Template not adapted, incomplete documentation
   825	
   826	---
   827	
   828	### Mistake 3: Deleting "Irrelevant" Sections
   829	
   830	**Wrong:**
   831	```markdown
   832	\## 1. OBJECTIVE
   833	[...]
   834	
   835	\## 3. IMPLEMENTATION
   836	[...]
   837	```
   838	
   839	**Right:**
   840	```markdown
   841	\## 1. OBJECTIVE
   842	[...]
   843	
   844	\## 2. SCOPE
   845	N/A - Single file change, no scope considerations
   846	
   847	\## 3. IMPLEMENTATION
   848	[...]
   849	```
   850	
   851	**Why wrong:** Breaks structure, loses numbering, unclear if section was forgotten or intentionally skipped
   852	
   853	---
   854	
   855	### Mistake 4: Generic Filenames
   856	
   857	**Wrong:**
   858	```bash
   859	decision-record-final.md
   860	```
   861	
   862	**Right:**
   863	```bash
   864	decision-record-database-choice.md
   865	```
   866	
   867	**Why wrong:** Not descriptive, unclear what decision is about
   868	
   869	---
   870	
   871	### Mistake 5: Skipping Cross-References
   872	
   873	**Wrong:**
   874	spec.md and plan.md exist but don't reference each other
   875	
   876	**Right:**
   877	```markdown
   878	<!-- In spec.md -->
   879	**Implementation Plan**: See [plan.md](plan.md) for detailed approach
   880	
   881	<!-- In plan.md -->
   882	**Requirements**: See [spec.md](spec.md) for complete specification
   883	```
   884	
   885	**Why wrong:** Documents feel disconnected, harder to navigate
   886	
   887	---
   888	
   889	## 9. TROUBLESHOOTING
   890	
   891	### "I don't know what to put in this section"
   892	
   893	**Solutions:**
   894	- If truly not applicable → Mark "N/A" with brief reason
   895	- If uncertain → Flag `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: ...]` and ask user
   896	- If blocked → Create research document to research and inform decision
   897	
   898	### "Template doesn't fit my feature"
   899	
   900	**Solutions:**
   901	- Use closest template as starting point
   902	- Adapt structure to fit (add subsections if needed)
   903	- Document modifications in changelog
   904	- Consider creating custom template for future use (consult user first)
   905	
   906	### "Should I include this in spec or plan?"
   907	
   908	**Rule of thumb:**
   909	- **spec.md** = WHAT and WHY (requirements, rationale, alternatives)
   910	- **plan.md** = HOW and WHEN (implementation steps, timeline, approach)
   911	
   912	**Example:**
   913	- "We need authentication" → spec.md
   914	- "We'll use OAuth 2.0" → spec.md (technical approach)
   915	- "Step 1: Install passport.js, Step 2: Configure routes..." → plan.md
   916	
   917	---
   918	
   919	## 10. USING SUB-FOLDERS FOR ORGANIZATION
   920	
   921	There are **two distinct sub-folder systems**:
   922	
   923	### 10.1 Workflow-Assisted Sub-Folder Versioning
   924	
   925	**Triggered when:** User selects Option A to reuse existing spec folder with root-level content.
   926	
   927	**How it works:**
   928	1. Workflow detects existing spec.md/plan.md at root level
   929	2. AI suggests sub-folder organization if appropriate
   930	3. User chooses a descriptive name for the new sub-folder
   931	4. Sub-folder created via `create.sh --subfolder` or manually
   932	5. Spec folder path passed via explicit CLI target
   933	6. Each sub-folder gets an independent `scratch/` workspace and `graph-metadata.json`
   934	
   935	Archival and reorganization of existing root content is explicit (user-driven), not automatic.
   936	
   937	**Example:**
   938	```text
   939	specs/122-skill-standardization/
   940	├── 001-original-work/  (manually organized)
   941	│   ├── spec.md
   942	│   └── plan.md
   943	├── 002-api-refactor/   (completed)
   944	│   └── ...
   945	└── 003-bug-fixes/      (current work - path passed via CLI)
   946	    ├── spec.md
   947	    ├── plan.md
   948	    ├── graph-metadata.json
   949	    └── scratch/
   950	```
   951	
   952	**See:** `system-spec-kit SKILL.md` Section 3 (Sub-Folder Versioning) for full versioning workflow.
   953	
   954	### 10.2 Manual Sub-Folders for Organization
   955	
   956	Create sub-folders **manually** within spec folders when:
   957	- **Complex umbrella projects** require organizing multiple related work streams
   958	- **Parallel work** on different components of the same feature
   959	- **Iterative analysis** needs separate workspace (e.g., alignment work, research phases)
   960	- **Keeping related artifacts together** under a parent spec
   961	
   962	### Sub-Folder Structure Pattern
   963	
   964	```text
   965	specs/###-parent-feature/
   966	  spec.md              # Parent feature specification
   967	  plan.md              # Overall implementation plan
   968	  README.md            # Optional: Parent overview (if sub-folders exist)
   969	
   970	  sub-analysis-1/
   971	    README.md          # Sub-folder purpose and organization
   972	    analysis.md        # Specific analysis work
   973	    findings.md        # Results and conclusions
   974	
   975	  sub-implementation-2/
   976	    README.md          # Sub-folder purpose and organization
   977	    component-spec.md  # Component-specific specification
   978	    testing-plan.md    # Component-specific testing
   979	
   980	  scratch/             # Temporary workspace (continuity lives in implementation-summary.md)
   981	    .gitkeep
   982	  graph-metadata.json  # Generated graph metadata
   983	```
   984	
   985	### Creating a Sub-Folder
   986	
   987	**1. Determine if sub-folder is appropriate:**
   988	- Does this work relate to a larger feature? (Use sub-folder)
   989	- Is this independent work? (Create new top-level spec folder)
   990	
   991	**2. Create sub-folder with descriptive name:**
   992	```bash
   993	# Example: Analysis work for skill standardization
   994	mkdir -p specs/122-skill-standardization/spec-enforcement-improvements
   995	```
   996	
   997	**3. Create README.md:**
   998	- Document the sub-folder's purpose
   999	- Link to parent spec
  1000	- Explain organization and structure
  1001	
  1002	**4. Fill out the README:**
  1003	- Parent spec reference (link to `../spec.md` or parent folder)
  1004	- Sub-folder purpose and scope
  1005	- Key documents and their roles
  1006	- Status and progress tracking
  1007	- References to related sub-folders (if applicable)
  1008	
  1009	### Sub-Folder Naming Conventions
  1010	
  1011	- **Lowercase with hyphens:** `spec-enforcement-improvements`, `cli-opencode-alignment`
  1012	- **Descriptive:** Clearly indicates the sub-folder's purpose
  1013	- **Consistent with sibling folders:** Follow established patterns in the parent spec
  1014	- **Avoid generic names:** `analysis`, `work` (too vague)
  1015	- **Use specific names:** `api-integration-analysis`, `performance-optimization-work`
  1016	
  1017	### Real-World Example
  1018	
  1019	**Parent Spec:** `specs/122-skill-standardization/`
  1020	**Purpose:** Standardize all skills across the project
  1021	
  1022	**Sub-Folders:**
  1023	```text
  1024	specs/122-skill-standardization/
  1025	  cli-opencode-alignment/
  1026	    README.md           # Purpose: Align cli-opencode skill with standards
  1027	    analysis.md         # Current state analysis
  1028	    changes_summary.md  # Changes needed
  1029	    validation_report.md # Post-change validation
  1030	
  1031	  cli-opencode-alignment/
  1032	    README.md           # Purpose: Align cli-opencode skill with standards
  1033	    analysis.md
  1034	    changes_summary.md
  1035	    validation_report.md
  1036	
  1037	  spec-enforcement-improvements/
  1038	    README.md           # Purpose: Improve spec folder template enforcement
  1039	    spec.md             # Feature specification (Level 2)
  1040	    plan.md             # Implementation plan
  1041	    validation-rules.md # Detailed validation logic
  1042	    testing_checklist.md # Test procedures
  1043	```
  1044	
  1045	**Benefits of this organization:**
  1046	- Clear separation of concerns (each skill gets own sub-folder)
  1047	- Consistent structure across sub-folders
  1048	- Easy navigation with README files
  1049	- Parent spec ties everything together
  1050	- Can work on sub-folders in parallel
  1051	
  1052	### When NOT to Use Sub-Folders
  1053	
  1054	**Create a new top-level spec folder instead when:**
  1055	- Work is independent from existing specs
  1056	- Feature doesn't relate to an umbrella project
  1057	- Sub-folder would have only 1-2 files (overkill for organization)
  1058	- Work deserves its own spec number for tracking
  1059	
  1060	**Use the parent spec folder directly when:**
  1061	- Simple feature with 2-5 related files
  1062	- No need for additional organization
  1063	- All work fits naturally in flat structure
  1064	
  1065	### Sub-Folder Validation
  1066	
  1067	The enforce-spec-folder workflow includes sub-folder detection:
  1068	- **Automatic suggestion:** When working in a sub-folder without README
  1069	- **Template recommendation:** Suggests creating a README.md to document the sub-folder
  1070	- **Non-blocking:** Suggestion only, not enforced
  1071	- **Skips scratch/ folder:** No README needed for the temporary workspace
  1072	
  1073	### Best Practices
  1074	
  1075	1. **Always create README first** - Documents purpose before diving into work
  1076	2. **Link to parent spec** - Maintain traceability with `../spec.md` references
  1077	3. **Use consistent naming** - Follow patterns established in parent or sibling sub-folders
  1078	4. **Update parent README** - If parent has README, list sub-folders there
  1079	5. **Keep sub-folders focused** - One clear purpose per sub-folder
  1080	6. **Clean up when complete** - Consider archiving or consolidating after work is done
  1081	
  1082	### Integration with Parent Spec
  1083	
  1084	**In parent spec.md:**
  1085	```markdown
  1086	## Related Work
  1087	
  1088	This feature includes work organized in sub-folders:
  1089	- `spec-enforcement-improvements/` - Template structure validation enhancements
  1090	- `template-marker-system/` - Template source tracking implementation
  1091	- `hybrid-validation/` - Existing vs new spec folder validation
  1092	
  1093	See each sub-folder's README.md for details.
  1094	```
  1095	
  1096	**In sub-folder README.md:**
  1097	```markdown
  1098	## Parent Spec
  1099	
  1100	- **Parent**: [Skill Standardization](../spec.md)
  1101	- **Related Sub-Folders**:
  1102	  - [template-marker-system](../template-marker-system/)
  1103	  - [hybrid-validation](../hybrid-validation/)
  1104	```
  1105	
  1106	---
  1107	
  1108	## 11. PHASE ORGANIZATION
  1109	
  1110	### Phase Template Addendums
  1111	
  1112	When a specification is decomposed into phases, templates are applied at two levels:
  1113	
  1114	**Parent folder:** Uses standard templates for its declared level, plus a Phase Documentation Map section added to `spec.md`. This map tracks all child phases, their status, and their descriptions.
  1115	
  1116	**Child phase folders:** Each child uses standard templates for its declared level (typically matching the parent level). Child `spec.md` files include an additional metadata field (`parent:`) that back-references the parent folder.
  1117	
  1118	### Phase-Specific Template Additions
  1119	
  1120	| Template | Phase Addition | Location |
  1121	|----------|---------------|----------|
  1122	| `spec.md` (parent) | Phase Documentation Map table | New section in parent spec |
  1123	| `spec.md` (child) | `parent:` and `phase:` metadata fields | YAML frontmatter or metadata block |
  1124	| `plan.md` (parent) | Phase Dependencies section | Documents cross-phase dependencies |
  1125	
  1126	### Creating Phase Folders
  1127	
  1128	```bash
  1129	# Create phase child folder with templates
  1130	.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh \
  1131	  --phase \
  1132	  --phases 3 \
  1133	  --phase-names foundation,implementation,integration \
  1134	  "Phase 1: Core data models"
  1135	```
  1136	
  1137	### Phase Validation
  1138	
  1139	Validate all phases recursively from the parent:
  1140	
  1141	```bash
  1142	bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/###-parent-feature/ --recursive
  1143	```
  1144	
  1145	This validates the parent and each child phase folder independently.
  1146	
  1147	### Full Documentation
  1148	
  1149	See [phase-definitions.md](../structure/phase-definitions.md) for complete phase system documentation.
  1150	
  1151	---
  1152	
  1153	## 12. RELATED RESOURCES
  1154	
  1155	### Reference Files
  1156	- [quick-reference.md](../workflows/quick-reference.md) - Commands, checklists, and troubleshooting
  1157	- [level-specifications.md](./level-specifications.md) - Complete Level 1-3 requirements and migration
  1158	- [path-scoped-rules.md](../validation/path-scoped-rules.md) - Path-scoped validation rules reference
  1159	
  1160	### Templates
  1161	
  1162	**Manifest Templates (Level-Gated):**
  1163	
  1164	Templates are stored as `*.md.tmpl` files and rendered by Level:
  1165	
  1166	| Level | Folder | Contents |
  1167	|-------|--------|----------|
  1168	| Level 1 | `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` | spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, implementation-summary.md |
  1169	| Level 2 | `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` | Level 1 + acceptance-criteria.md |
  1170	| Level 3 | `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` | Level 2 file set; decision-record.md and research/research.md stay lazy add-ons |
  1171	| Level 3+ | `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` | Level 3 + governance sections |
  1172	| Phase Parent | `templates/packet-types/phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl` | lean parent spec.md |
  1173	
  1174	**Level 1 Templates:**
  1175	- [spec template](../../templates/core/spec.md.tmpl) - Requirements and user stories template
  1176	- [plan.md](../../templates/core/plan.md.tmpl) - Technical implementation plan template
  1177	- [tasks.md](../../templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl) - Task breakdown template
  1178	- [implementation-summary.md](../../templates/core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl) - Post-implementation summary
  1179	
  1180	**Level 2 Templates (includes Level 1 content):**
  1181	- [acceptance-criteria.md](../../templates/addons/acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl) - the Level 2+ closure gate
  1182	
  1183	**Level 3 Templates (includes Level 2 content):**
  1184	- [decision-record.md](../../templates/addons/decision-record.md.tmpl) - Architecture Decision Records template
  1185	- [research.md.tmpl](../../templates/addons/research.md.tmpl) - Render to `research/research.md` when Level 3 research is needed
  1186	
  1187	**Cross-Level Templates (at templates root):**
  1188	- [handover.md.tmpl](../../templates/addons/handover.md.tmpl) - Full session handover document (~100-150 lines)
  1189	- [debug-delegation.md.tmpl](../../templates/addons/debug-delegation.md.tmpl) - Debug task delegation for sub-agents
  1190	
  1191	**Non-Template Folders (for reference):**
  1192	- `scratch/` - Temporary workspace folder (create ad-hoc files as needed, no template)
  1193	- Canonical continuity lives inside packet docs, primarily `_memory.continuity` in `implementation-summary.md`
  1194	
  1195	### Related Skills
  1196	- `sk-code` - Implementation, debugging, and verification lifecycle
  1197	- `system-spec-kit` - Context preservation with semantic memory
  1198	- `sk-git` - Git workspace setup and clean commits
  1199	
  1200	---

