minRounds\": 2|\"convergenceMode\": \"default\"|\"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/deep-ai-council-config.json`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/cross-mode-anti-convergence-contract.md:51:2. `bash: rg -n '\"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"|minRounds|maxRounds|invariants' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/cross-mode-anti-convergence-contract.md:52:3. `bash: rg -n 'missing stopPolicy|stopPolicy must be \"fail-closed\"|validateStopPolicy' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/cross-mode-anti-convergence-contract.md:53:4. `bash: rg -n 'antiConvergence.convergenceMode|convergenceMode|minIterations<=maxIterations|minIterations|maxIterations' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/cross-mode-anti-convergence-contract.md:74:| DAC-033 | Cross-mode anti-convergence contract | Verify council min-round floor and fail-closed guards | `Check whether deep-ai-council has a minimum round floor and fail-closed stop policy before convergence is trusted.` | `bash: rg -n '\"antiConvergence\"|\"minRounds\": 2|\"convergenceMode\": \"default\"|\"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/deep-ai-council-config.json -> bash: rg -n '\"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"|minRounds|maxRounds|invariants' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/runtime-capabilities.json -> bash: rg -n 'missing stopPolicy|stopPolicy must be \"fail-closed\"|validateStopPolicy' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/runtime-capabilities.cjs -> bash: rg -n 'antiConvergence.convergenceMode|convergenceMode|minIterations<=maxIterations|minIterations|maxIterations' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json` | Council config, runtime matrix, resolver, and optimizer anchors present | Grep output lines | PASS if explicit | Inspect config, then runtime matrix |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/cross-mode-anti-convergence-contract.md:91:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/deep-ai-council-config.json` | Council anti-convergence config |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/cross-mode-anti-convergence-contract.md:92:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/runtime-capabilities.json` | Council runtime capability policy and invariant names |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/cross-mode-anti-convergence-contract.md:93:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/runtime-capabilities.cjs` | Shared fail-closed stop-policy validation |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/cross-mode-anti-convergence-contract.md:94:| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json` | Shared anti-convergence optimizer invariant group |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:3:description: \"Package index for the deep-alignment conformance_benchmark family: each benchmark-id directory binds a canonical corpus to a named authority and peer adapter, with its lane config, independent fixtures, status, source packet, execution command, and run-evidence location. Currently indexes the command-surface benchmark (sk-doc authority, sk-doc-command adapter).\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:7:  - \"command surface conformance benchmark family\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:20:`the OpenCode command surface — canonical command sources, their declared workflow\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:27:**Package status:** Authored and runnable — the `command-surface` inputs\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:30:over the command surface (overall verdict FAIL, with open findings); a formally\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:33:**Source specification:** `.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/066-command-surface-benchmark/`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:44:| [`command-surface`](./command-surface/conformance-benchmark.md) | `sk-doc` | `sk-doc-command` | `.opencode/commands` tree (public + held-out fixtures) | Live convergence run complete (FAIL); fixture-run identity pending | `system-deep-loop/066-command-surface-benchmark` | [command](#exec-command-surface) | [`004/alignment/`](../../../../../specs/system-deep-loop/066-command-surface-benchmark/004-command-lane-integration/alignment) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:50:| `command-surface` | `.opencode/commands` | Canonical command sources plus their generated mirrors and declared workflow/presentation assets, discovered under the lane scope; excludes runtime behavior and parameterized targets | [`fixture-manifest.json`](./command-surface/fixtures/fixture-manifest.json) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:58:<a id=\"exec-command-surface\"></a>\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:59:### exec-command-surface — `command-surface`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:65:/deep:alignment :auto --lane-config .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/command-surface/lane-config.json --spec-folder .opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/066-command-surface-benchmark/004-command-lane-integration\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:70:- Contract: [`command-surface/conformance-benchmark.md`](./command-surface/conformance-benchmark.md)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:71:- Lane config: [`command-surface/lane-config.json`](./command-surface/lane-config.json)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:72:- Fixture manifest: [`command-surface/fixtures/fixture-manifest.json`](./command-surface/fixtures/fixture-manifest.json)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:76:The package is the stable authoring surface; it is not the audit trail. Evidence\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:77:for `command-surface` lands at\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:78:[`004-command-lane-integration/alignment/`](../../../../../specs/system-deep-loop/066-command-surface-benchmark/004-command-lane-integration/alignment)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:85:- [`command-surface/conformance-benchmark.md`](./command-surface/conformance-benchmark.md) — the per-benchmark purpose, scope, inputs, validity gates, and ownership boundary.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:86:- [`command-surface/lane-config.json`](./command-surface/lane-config.json) — the deep-alignment lane selection.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/assets/conformance-benchmark/README.md:87:- [`command-surface/fixtures/fixture-manifest.json`](./command-surface/fixtures/fixture-manifest.json) — independent oracle provenance and fixture expectations.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json:57:  \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json:58:  \"reducerScriptPath\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json:92:    \"manifestPath\": \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/tests/orchestrate-session-cli.vitest.ts:140:  it.each(['cli-opencode', 'cli-claude-code'])(\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/tests/orchestrate-session-cli.vitest.ts:162:          executor: { kind: 'cli-opencode', model: family },\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/tests/orchestrate-session-cli.vitest.ts:222:      const seats = [{ id: 'seat-001', lens: 'Analytical', role: 'Implementation realist', vantage: 'cli-opencode' }];\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/tests/orchestrate-session-cli.vitest.ts:253:      expect(spawns[0].command).toBe('opencode');\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/tests/orchestrate-session-cli.vitest.ts:309:        executor: { kind: 'cli-opencode', model: 'provider/session-default' },\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/tests/orchestrate-session-cli.vitest.ts:330:      expect(spawns.flatMap(({ args }) => args)).not.toContain('cli-opencode');\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/tests/orchestrate-session-cli.vitest.ts:338:      const executablePath = join(binDir, 'opencode');\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/tests/orchestrate-session-cli.vitest.ts:366:          executor: { kind: 'cli-opencode', model: 'provider/test-model' },\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/rollback-failed-round-preserves-forensic-trail.md:88:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/rollback.js` | Rollback behavior |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/rollback-failed-round-preserves-forensic-trail.md:89:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md` | Failed folder layout |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/rollback-failed-round-preserves-forensic-trail.md:90:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/state-format.md` | Rollback state events |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/deep-loop-mode-classification/deep-loop-mode-classification.md:20:The `/deep:*` commands and native agent types are complementary surfaces that reach the same packets through their own static routers or agent definitions — they do not bypass or duplicate the registry.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/deep-loop-mode-classification/deep-loop-mode-classification.md:32:The advisor routes any deep-loop query to the single identity `system-deep-loop`; the hub then classifies intent to a `workflowMode` (a mode hint like `\"research: ...\"` overrides), guards `mode-registry.json`, and loads the resolved packet. It omits `discover_markdown_resources` and never selects hub-level `references/<key>/` or `assets/<key>/` resources by runtime key. A second-layer surface router at `shared/references/smart-routing.md` (mirroring the equivalent surfaces in `sk-prompt` and `sk-code`) maps a resolved mode's intent to packet-qualified child leaves for router-replay benchmarking; it never re-decides the mode and is not itself a runtime discovery surface.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/deep-loop-mode-classification/deep-loop-mode-classification.md:42:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md` | Shared | States the registry-driven classification contract and the three-tier discriminator. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/deep-loop-mode-classification/deep-loop-mode-classification.md:43:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json` | Shared | Declarative registry for all seven `workflowMode` packets. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/deep-loop-mode-classification/deep-loop-mode-classification.md:44:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/references/smart-routing.md` | Shared | Second-layer intent-to-leaf mapping consumed by router-replay benchmarking. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/deep-loop-mode-classification/deep-loop-mode-classification.md:50:| `.opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs` | Automated test | Structural hub conformance, including the tool-surface-union invariant this hub's broad `allowed-tools` grant satisfies. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/convergence/depth-dispatch.md:23:Use `/deep:ai-council:auto` for non-interactive bounded runs when setup answers are pre-bound, and `/deep:ai-council:confirm` when the operator should approve setup, loop, synthesis, and save gates. The command Markdown owns setup resolution and then loads `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-ai-council-auto.yaml` or `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-ai-council-confirm.yaml` for execution.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/convergence/depth-dispatch.md:35:Default cost guards are intentionally conservative: `max_rounds_per_topic = 3`, `max_topics_per_session = 5`, `saturation_threshold = 0.20`, and three seats per round. The default upper bound is 45 seat outputs, but stable verdict deltas should stop topics earlier. Operators may tune these values through command setup answers, and `:auto` must surface the computed upper bound before dispatch.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/convergence/depth-dispatch.md:288:cli-opencode agreed with cli-opencode.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/convergence/depth-dispatch.md:299:- Agent body: `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md` §0 ILLEGAL NESTING and §5 PARALLEL VS SEQUENTIAL.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-dashboard.md:24:2. **Recovery surface**, second recovery channel alongside JSONL after context compaction\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-dashboard.md:134:- Target: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research (skill)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-dashboard.md:157:- agent_cross_runtime protocol partial: OpenCode runtime path still unverified\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/README.md:67:node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs <spec-folder>\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/README.md:186:python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/README.md --type readme\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:16:    \"packetSkillName\": \"The packet's SKILL.md name. Most packets use folder == packetSkillName == deep-<mode> (e.g. deep-ai-council). Exception: the three improvement lanes (agent/skill/model) multiplex onto one shared packet 'deep-improvement', so several workflowModes map to that single folder/packetSkillName. The legacy public key 'ai-council' is preserved only on the command/agent surfaces, not on the packet folder/name.\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:17:    \"driftGuard\": \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/routing-registry-drift-guard.vitest.ts\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:26:      \"driftGuard\": \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/routing-registry-drift-guard.vitest.ts\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:37:      \"toolSurface\": {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:61:      \"toolSurface\": {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:85:      \"toolSurface\": {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:109:      \"toolSurface\": {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:135:      \"toolSurface\": {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:158:      \"toolSurface\": {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:181:      \"toolSurface\": {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/behavior-benchmark/framework.md:5:  that measure executor-model behavior at the deep-loop command surface under\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/behavior-benchmark/framework.md:13:  - command surface benchmark methodology\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/behavior-benchmark/framework.md:24:when its command surface is triggered with a realistic user prompt. The unit of\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/behavior-benchmark/framework.md:35:| `feature_catalog` | What **exists** in this skill (commands, surfaces, artifacts)? Inventory, not measurement. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/behavior-benchmark/framework.md:37:| `/deep:model-benchmark` | **Model** scoring against static fixtures. Fixed inputs, reproducible targets, no live command surface. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/behavior-benchmark/framework.md:38:| `behavior_benchmark` | **Live executor behavior at the real command surface** under realistic prompting. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/behavior-benchmark/framework.md:75:| `entry_surface` | enum | `E1` \\| `E2` \\| `E3` \\| `E4` (see below). |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/behavior-benchmark/framework.md:90:### Entry-surface codes\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:15:This catalog inventories the live `system-deep-loop` hub surface. The hub classifies a request into one of seven `workflowMode` packets (`research`, `review`, `ai-council`, `alignment`, and the three improvement lanes) through a three-tier discriminator, holding no per-mode logic itself. An opt-in, flag-gated compiled-routing fast path can resolve the same decision ahead of this registry-driven classification without changing what it resolves to.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:21:Use this catalog as the current-state inventory for the `system-deep-loop` hub. The hub classifies intent and loads the resolved packet; the `/deep:*` commands and native agent types are complementary surfaces that reach the same packets through their own static routers.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:35:`runtimeLoopType` is the graph-backed convergence key consumed by `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs`, explicitly `null` for the three improvement lanes rather than inferred; `backendKind` splits `runtime-loop-type` (research/review/ai-council/alignment) from `improvement-host` (the three improvement lanes). A second-layer surface router at `shared/references/smart-routing.md` supports router-replay benchmarking without re-deciding the mode.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:53:The directive is off by default: `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` is unset in normal operation, so `system-deep-loop` continues to classify entirely through `mode-registry.json`. When the flag is force-enabled and `system-deep-loop`'s promoted activation manifest authorizes compiled serving, `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub system-deep-loop --prompt \"<task>\"` returns the authoritative decision instead; any error or a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel leaves routing unchanged.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:11:  sourceOfTruth: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:48:      description: Review a named agent across runtime-specific definitions and capability parity surfaces.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:248:      passCriteria: Feature catalog claims match current capability, entry points, and discoverable implementation surfaces.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:381:      path: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract-snapshot.md\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:383:      generator: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/render-contract-snapshot.cjs\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:409:    path: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:419:    path: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-confirm.yaml\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:428:  - id: agent-opencode\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:429:    path: .opencode/agents/deep-review.md\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:436:    note: Hand-maintained OpenCode agent definition. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml:447:    path: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/quick-reference.md\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/max-rounds-without-convergence-emits-non-converged.md:49:1. `bash: rg -