testing-playbook/state-and-fault-tolerance/state-machine-wiring-regression.md:51:4. `bash: rg -n 'NFR-R01|documented manual coverage check|Option A|extend the enum|Do not silently reuse' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/references/state-machine-wiring.md .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/scripts/check-convergence.cjs`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/manual-testing-playbook/state-and-fault-tolerance/state-machine-wiring-regression.md:75:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/scripts/tests/state-machine-wiring.test.cjs` | The end-to-end wiring regression (4 tests) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/manual-testing-playbook/state-and-fault-tolerance/state-machine-wiring-regression.md:76:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/references/state-machine-wiring.md` | §2 state-to-script map; §5 loopType decision |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/manual-testing-playbook/state-and-fault-tolerance/state-machine-wiring-regression.md:77:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/scripts/check-convergence.cjs` | Header documents the NFR-R01 self-contained coverage check |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/manual-testing-playbook/state-and-fault-tolerance/state-machine-wiring-regression.md:78:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` | The shared engine whose loopType enum excludes \"alignment\" |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/writer-library-contract/out-of-scope-write-rejection.md:29:The shipped surface is anchored by `deep-ai-council`. The playbook scenario `writer-library-contract/out-of-scope-write-rejection.md` defines the operator prompt, command sequence, expected signals, evidence, and pass/fail criteria for DAC-017.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/writer-library-contract/out-of-scope-write-rejection.md:31:Current behavior is grounded in `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/persist-artifacts.cjs`, which the scenario identifies as path guard implementation. Validation is anchored by `manual-testing-playbook/writer-library-contract/out-of-scope-write-rejection.md`, covering manual scenario contract.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/writer-library-contract/out-of-scope-write-rejection.md:43:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/persist-artifacts.cjs` | Library | Path guard implementation |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/writer-library-contract/out-of-scope-write-rejection.md:44:| `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md` | Runtime Mirror | Scoped-write authority declaration |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:22:`@deep-ai-council` is planning-only. It returns a council report and cannot write, edit, patch, or run shell commands. The dispatching parent owns persistence by invoking `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs` after the report is captured.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:50:`cli-claude-code`, `cli-opencode`, and `cli-opencode` playbooks may capture a council report from an external runtime and then invoke the same helper locally. Each playbook stays within ONE CLI per round (`SKILL.md §4` ALWAYS rule 6); multi-CLI deliberations stage additional dedicated rounds.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:74:node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs \"$PACKET\" \\\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:80:node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/memory/generate-context.js \\\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:112:      node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:122:      node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/memory/generate-context.js\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:160:The helper exits `1` when required report sections are missing. It exits `2` when artifact or payload writes partially fail. Callers should surface that status and avoid running `generate-context.js` if the payload file was not written.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:165:node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/advise-council-completion.cjs \"$PACKET\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:174:- Agent body §16: `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:175:- Output schema: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:176:- State format: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/state-format.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:177:- Persistence helper: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md:178:- Memory save entrypoint: `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/memory/generate-context.js`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/council-graph-integration/council-graph-convergence-three-state-decision-matrix.md:96:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` | runtime CLI script: three-state decision logic |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/council-graph-integration/council-graph-convergence-three-state-decision-matrix.md:97:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/council/council-graph-query.ts` | Per-signal helpers (`agreementRatio`, `dissentDensity`, etc.) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/council-graph-integration/council-graph-convergence-three-state-decision-matrix.md:98:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/council-graph-script.vitest.ts` | Tests: \"allows convergence when ... thresholds are met\", \"continues convergence when non-blocking thresholds are not met\", \"blocks convergence for empty derived graphs...\" |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/council-graph-integration/council-graph-convergence-three-state-decision-matrix.md:99:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/integration/graph-support.md` §4 | Documents the convergence signals |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/lane-resolution/scope-types.md:21:A lane's scope answers \"where to look.\" It is the third axis of the scoping tree, and it is the only axis with a security surface: an unvalidated scope value could point a lane outside the workspace before any adapter's `discover()` ever ran, so scope validation is a hard containment boundary, not a formatting nicety.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/RVB-007-delegation-route-proof.md:8:  \"entry_surface\": \"E1\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/RVB-007-delegation-route-proof.md:10:  \"prompt\": \".opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-001-review-target :auto --review-target-type=spec-folder --dims=all --max-iterations=1 --convergence=0.0 --stop-policy=max-iterations --spec-folder=.opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmark