the adapter cites |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/manual-testing-playbook/report-emission-per-lane/one-report-per-lane.md:48:1. `bash: rg -n 'renderAlignmentReport|## Lane:|one report per lane|Never manually edited|Emit one report per lane' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-alignment-state.cjs .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/SKILL.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/manual-testing-playbook/report-emission-per-lane/one-report-per-lane.md:49:2. `bash: D=$(mktemp -d); mkdir -p \"$D/alignment/deltas\"; L1=\"sk-doc::docs::docs/\"; L2=\"sk-git::git-history::main..HEAD\"; printf '{\"alignmentTarget\":\"fx\",\"lanes\":[{\"authority\":\"sk-doc\",\"artifactClass\":\"docs\",\"scope\":{\"type\":\"paths\",\"values\":[\"docs/\"]}},{\"authority\":\"sk-git\",\"artifactClass\":\"git-history\",\"scope\":{\"type\":\"branchRange\",\"from\":\"main\",\"to\":\"HEAD\"}}]}' > \"$D/alignment/deep-alignment-config.json\"; printf '{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"laneId\":\"%s\",\"artifactsChecked\":1,\"newFindingsRatio\":1}\\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"laneId\":\"%s\",\"artifactsChecked\":1,\"newFindingsRatio\":1}\\n' \"$L1\" \"$L2\" > \"$D/alignment/deep-alignment-state.jsonl\"; printf '{\"type\":\"finding\",\"laneId\":\"%s\",\"finding\":{\"severity\":\"P1\",\"type\":\"missing-required-section\",\"message\":\"doc gap\",\"artifactPath\":\"docs/a.md\"}}\\n' \"$L1\" > \"$D/alignment/deltas/iter-001.jsonl\"; printf '{\"type\":\"finding\",\"laneId\":\"%s\",\"finding\":{\"severity\":\"P0\",\"type\":\"invalid-subject-format\",\"message\":\"bad commit\",\"artifactRef\":\"abc123\"}}\\n' \"$L2\" > \"$D/alignment/deltas/iter-002.jsonl\"; node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-alignment-state.cjs \"$D\" >/dev/null; sed -n '1,80p' \"$D/alignment/alignment-report.md\"`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/manual-testing-playbook/report-emission-per-lane/one-report-per-lane.md:73:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-alignment-state.cjs` | `renderAlignmentReport` one-section-per-lane output |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/manual-testing-playbook/report-emission-per-lane/one-report-per-lane.md:74:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/SKILL.md` | ALWAYS-#5 (one report per lane, not blended) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/improvement-lane-routing/skill-benchmark.md:52:1. `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json` contains the `skill-benchmark` mode entry.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/improvement-lane-routing/skill-benchmark.md:57:1. **Invoke command surface**: enter the exact prompt into the orchestrator runtime.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/improvement-lane-routing/skill-benchmark.md:65:| 1 | Command surface selects `/deep:skill-benchmark`. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/improvement-lane-routing/skill-benchmark.md:84:- `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md` - improvement family routing rule.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/improvement-lane-routing/skill-benchmark.md:85:- `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json` - `skill-benchmark` source of truth.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:17:The manual testing playbook (`manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`) is the companion validation surface: every feature here maps to a DAC scenario there. Feature IDs use the `DAC-NNN` prefix.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:40:| Advisor routes council prompts to skill | The skill advisor scorer surfaces `deep-ai-council` for council prompts. | [runtime-routing-and-rename/advisor-routes-council-prompts-to-skill.md](../feature-catalog/runtime-routing-and-rename/advisor-routes-council-prompts-to-skill.md) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:117:Scenario IDs: DAC-019..DAC-026. The runtime council graph CLI surface, derived-projection guarantees, and retired MCP registry entries.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:128:| Council graph MCP surface retired | Council graph operations are absent from system-spec-memory and available through `runtime/ --loop-type council`. | [council-graph-integration/council-graph-tools-registered-separately-from-deep-loop.md](../feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-tools-registered-separately-from-deep-loop.md) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:142:| Hot-topic discovery | `hot_nodes` mode surfaces high-degree contested topics; the baseline needs manual tallying. | [council-graph-value-comparison/hot-topic-discovery-graph-vs-baseline.md](../feature-catalog/council-graph-value-comparison/hot-topic-discovery-graph-vs-baseline.md) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-git.md:21:`sk-git.cjs` wraps real `git` commands plus a line-cited port of `.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/commit-msg`'s structural grammar. It is 100% deterministic (ADR-004) — both checked dimensions are regex/lookup-checkable against live git state with no judgment call, so it has no reasoning-agent layer, unlike sk-doc's two-layer shape.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-git.md:29:**Difference from deep-review:** deep-review never audits git history — it has no commit-grammar or branch-naming dimension and no `branchRange` scope. sk-git-adapter is the only adapter whose artifacts are refs rather than files, and the only one whose entire check surface is deterministic with zero reasoning-agent layer.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-git.md:42:| `.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/commit-msg` | Standard source | The live enforcement hook whose grammar is ported line-for-line. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-git.md:43:| `.opencode/skills/sk-git/SKILL.md` | Standard source | The `wt/{NNNN}-{name}` rule (line 298) and the commit-message logic the port cites. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/cross-reference-verification-detects-misalignment.md:48:1. `bash: rg -n 'crossReference|cross_reference|spec_code|checklist_evidence|skill_agent|agent_cross_runtime|feature_catalog_code|playbook_capability' .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/cross-reference-verification-detects-misalignment.md:49:2. `bash: rg -n 'traceability|cross.reference|TRACEABILITY PROTOCOLS' .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/cross-reference-verification-detects-misalignment.md:50:3. `bash: rg -n 'cross.reference|traceability|spec_code|checklist_evidence' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/quick-reference.md .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/cross-reference-verification-detects-misalignment.md:74:| `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml` | Config creation and dispatch, inspect `step_create_config` crossReference block and dispatch traceability constraints |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/cross-reference-verification-detects-misalignment.md:75:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml` | Cross-reference protocol definitions, inspect `cross_reference_protocols` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/cross-reference-verification-detects-misalignment.md:76:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/quick-reference.md` | Quality guards, use `ANCHOR:quality-guards` and `ANCHOR:review-dimensions` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/cross-reference-verification-detects-misalignment.md:77:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md` | Traceability dimension documentation |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/cross-reference-verification-detects-misalignment.md:87:- Feature catalog status: No `feature-catalog/` package exists under `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/` as of 2026-03-28.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:15:This playbook package adopts the typed per-scenario split-document pattern. The root document acts as the directory, review surface, and orchestration guide; each per-scenario file in the category folders carries typed routing gold in its YAML frontmatter plus the full execution contract in its body.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:42:2. The orchestrator consults the skill advisor, command router, or explicit Skill invocation and decides whether to invoke the hub, a `/deep:*` command surface, another skill, or no deep-loop workflow.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:43:3. The operator captures: which skill won the advisor vote, which `workflowMode` was selected, which command and agent surface would be used, which backend was resolved, which artifact root was named, and what the AI's response actually was.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:60:2. The hub skill is present at `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:61:3. `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md` states that `mode-registry.json` is the single source of truth and that the hub holds no per-mode convergence, state, or synthesis logic.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:62:4. `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json` contains exactly 7 active modes in its `modes` array.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:63:5. The skill advisor at `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_advisor.py` is callable when advisor scenarios are executed.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:85:- Skill advisor probe: `python3 .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_advisor.py \"<prompt>\" --threshold 0.8`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:87:- Command-surface invocation: enter the exact `/deep:*` command and prompt into the orchestrator runtime.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:88:- Registry check: read `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json` and compare the selected mode to the matching `modes[]` entry.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:89:- Resource path notation: paths shown relative to `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/` unless explicitly stated otherwise.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:166:| `AI-001` | Single Advisor Identity | Positive deep-loop controls surface `system-deep-loop` as the hub identity | `advisor-integration/single-advisor-identity.md` | Yes |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:193:Automated drift guards may exist for advisor projection maps, but this playbook is the manual validation surface for operator-observed routing behavior. Do not treat an automated guard as a substitute for the scenario transcripts unless the feature file explicitly allows the automated output as supporting evidence.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:211:(no root `Feature ID | file | Yes/No` cross-reference table); the surface router\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-design-live-render.md:41:| `.opencode/skills/sk-design/design-audit/references/accessibility-performance.md` | Standard source | The concrete-thresholds table the `THRESHOLDS` constant cites verbatim. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:48:1. `bash: rg -n 'step_generate_dashboard|dashboard' .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:49:2. `bash: sed -n '1,220p' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-dashboard.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:50:3. `bash: rg -n 'dashboard|deep-review-dashboard' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/quick-reference.md .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-confirm.yaml`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:74:| `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml` | Dashboard generation step, inspect `step_generate_dashboard` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:75:| `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-confirm.yaml` | Dashboard generation step, inspect `step_generate_dashboard` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:76:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-dashboard.md` | Dashboard template |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:77:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/quick-reference.md` | State files table, use `ANCHOR:state-files` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-dashboard-generation-after-iteration.md:87:- Feature catalog status: No `feature-catalog/` package exists under `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/` as of 2026-03-28.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-upsert-idempotency-and-self-loop-rejection.md:29:The shipped surface is anchored by `runtime upsert CLI`, `runtime status CLI`. The playbook scenario `council-graph-integration/council-graph-upsert-idempotency-and-self-loop-rejection.md` defines the operator prompt, command sequence, expected signals, evidence, and pass/fail criteria for DAC-019.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-upsert-idempotency-and-self-loop-rejection.md:31:Current behavior is grounded in `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`, which the scenario identifies as runtime CLI script: idempotent upser