e/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-upsert-empty-input-no-op-success.md:29:The shipped surface is anchored by `runtime upsert CLI`, `runtime status CLI`, `deep-ai-council`. The playbook scenario `council-graph-integration/council-graph-upsert-empty-input-no-op-success.md` defines the operator prompt, command sequence, expected signals, evidence, and pass/fail criteria for DAC-020.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-upsert-empty-input-no-op-success.md:31:Current behavior is grounded in `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`, which the scenario identifies as runtime CLI script: explicit empty-input no-op branch (p1-001 remediation). Validation is anchored by `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/council-graph-script.vitest.ts`, covering test: \"treats empty upsert as an explicit no-op success\".\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-upsert-empty-input-no-op-success.md:43:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs` | Handler | runtime CLI script: explicit empty-input no-op branch (P1-001 remediation) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-upsert-empty-input-no-op-success.md:50:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/council-graph-script.vitest.ts` | Automated test | Test: \"treats empty upsert as an explicit no-op success\" |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-iteration-reads-state-before-review.md:48:1. `bash: rg -n 'step_read_state|current_iteration|next_focus|Read.*state' .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-confirm.yaml`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-iteration-reads-state-before-review.md:49:2. `bash: rg -n 'Read.*state\\|Read.*strategy\\|Read.*JSONL\\|step 1\\|1\\. Read' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/quick-reference.md .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-iteration-reads-state-before-review.md:50:3. `bash: sed -n '1,220p' .opencode/agents/deep-review.md && sed -n '1,220p' .claude/agents/deep-review.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-iteration-reads-state-before-review.md:74:| `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml` | Loop state extraction, inspect `step_read_state` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-iteration-reads-state-before-review.md:75:| `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-confirm.yaml` | Loop state extraction, inspect `step_read_state` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-iteration-reads-state-before-review.md:76:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/quick-reference.md` | Iteration checklist, use `ANCHOR:agent-iteration-checklist` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-iteration-reads-state-before-review.md:77:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md` | Skill-level iteration documentation |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-iteration-reads-state-before-review.md:78:| `.opencode/agents/deep-review.md` | OpenCode runtime agent sequence, inspect iteration protocol |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/review-iteration-reads-state-before-review.md:89:- Feature catalog status: No `feature-catalog/` package exists under `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/` as of 2026-03-28.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:3:description: \"The hybrid authority adapter that surface-detects code artifacts and runs the real per-surface drift tooling plus a reasoning-agent dispatch layer for the code artifact-class.\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:6:  - \"surface detection stack_detection\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:8:  - \"webflow minification verification\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:19:The hybrid authority adapter that surface-detects code artifacts and runs the real per-surface drift tooling plus a reasoning-agent dispatch layer for the `code` artifact-class.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:21:`sk-code.cjs` is the hardest, least-deterministic adapter (ADR-008: HYBRID). It wraps the real sk-code surface-detection router and the real deterministic drift tooling, and builds a documented dispatch packet for everything that tooling structurally cannot check. Every finding is tagged `deterministic` or `reasoning-agent` — no false determinism.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:25:`discover()` walks code files (the OpenCode-checkable extension set plus CSS/HTML), reading each candidate's content because `stack-detection.md`'s WEBFLOW detection order includes a content-grep fallback a path-only classifier cannot reproduce. It classifies each artifact's surface (OPENCODE highest precedence, then WEBFLOW path/filename/content markers, else UNKNOWN) and flags a MOTION_DEV overlay signal. `standardSource('sk-code')` returns the surface router, the per-surface validators, an `excludedFromCheck` record for the tree-mutating `minify-webflow.mjs`, and the reference dirs. `check()` runs a surface-routed deterministic layer — `verify_alignment_drift.py --root` for OPENCODE (ERROR → P0, WARN → P1; a non-covered extension yields a `deterministic-layer-not-applicable` P2), and `verify-minification.mjs`/`test-minified-runtime.mjs` for WEBFLOW when a real project root is discoverable (FAIL → P0; otherwise an honest `deterministic-layer-unavailable` fallback per NFR-R01) — plus a reasoning-agent `checkPatternConformance()` layer. That layer is verify-first: `buildReasoningLayerDispatch()` prepares which dimensions to judge and which references to read, but the `.cjs` never judges itself; it only translates confirmed, cited contradictions the caller feeds back into findings.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:27:The adapter deliberately excludes `minify-webflow.mjs` from `check()` because it writes `z_minified/*.min.js` and a manifest, which would violate the read-only default; a documented spec-vs-tool extension-set discrepancy (Rust) is recorded rather than silently resolved.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:39:| `scripts/adapters/sk-code.cjs` | Adapter | `discover`/`standardSource`/`check`, the ported surface classifier, per-surface subprocess wrappers, and `buildReasoningLayerDispatch()`. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:40:| `references/adapters/sk-code-adapter.md` | Reference | Full specification: surface classifier provenance, the two deterministic surfaces (Section 4.1), the reasoning-agent dispatch (ADR-008). |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:42:| `.opencode/skills/sk-code/code-opencode/assets/scripts/verify_alignment_drift.py` | Wrapped tool | The OPENCODE deterministic drift checker. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/feature-catalog/adapter-contract/adapter-sk-code.md:43:| `.opencode/skills/sk-code/code-webflow/assets/scripts/verify-minification.mjs` | Wrapped tool | The WEBFLOW minification-pattern-preservation checker (read-only). |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-query-hostile-metadata-redaction.md:29:The shipped surface is anchored by `runtime upsert CLI`, `runtime query CLI`, `deep-ai-council`. The playbook scenario `council-graph-integration/council-graph-query-hostile-metadata-redaction.md` defines the operator prompt, command sequence, expected signals, evidence, and pass/fail criteria for DAC-021.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-query-hostile-metadata-redaction.md:31:Current behavior is grounded in `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/council/council-graph-query.ts`, which the scenario identifies as allowlist + length bounds (p1-003 remediation). Validation is anchored by `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/council-graph-script.vitest.ts`, covering test: \"redacts arbitrary metadata from prompt-safe query output\".\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-query-hostile-metadata-redaction.md:43:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/council/council-graph-query.ts` | Library | Allowlist + length bounds (P1-003 remediation) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-query-hostile-metadata-redaction.md:44:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/query.cjs` | Handler | runtime CLI script: prompt-safe query envelope |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-query-hostile-metadata-redaction.md:45:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/integration/graph-support.md` | Reference | Documents the allowlist contract |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-query-hostile-metadata-redaction.md:52:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/council-graph-script.vitest.ts` | Automated test | Test: \"redacts arbitrary metadata from prompt-safe query output\" |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/graph-events-review.md:51:1. `bash: rg -n 'graphEvents|review iteration records|graph-aware review convergence' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/graph-events-review.md:52:2. `bash: rg -n \"LoopType|loop_type.*review|coverage_nodes|coverage_edges\" .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/graph-events-review.md:53:3. `bash: rg -n 'graphEvents|loop_type|review' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/tests/coverage-graph-convergence.vitest.ts`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/graph-events-review.md:76:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md` | Graph-aware review convergence contract, documents `graphEvents` as iteration-record input |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/manual-testing-playbook/iteration-execution-and-state-discipline/graph-events-revi