val-loop/scripts/converge.cjs:96:    total_dispatches: totalDispatches,\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-06-02--minimax-capability-discrimination--mimo/eval/strict-validation/synthesis.md:3:> Real run: 4 validation-heavy fixtures × 2 models × 5 samples = 40 cells, `--variant high`, completed 2026-06-02 in ~29 min. 0 dispatch failures, 0 repo pollution, 0 orphans. The machine `## Trust verdict` (below) prints \"TIE-on-format\"; that is a **saturation artifact** — the real, gate-based reading follows.\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-06-02--minimax-capability-discrimination--mimo/eval/strict-validation/synthesis.md:35:The n=2 de-risk briefly showed the *opposite* (M3 0.87 on ipv4, MiMo 1.0) and suggested \"complementary blips, near-equivalent.\" That was a small-sample artifact: M3's one ipv4 score was a rare 1-in-7 truncation (8-word output) that did **not** recur across 5 samples, while MiMo's first two ipv4 samples happened to be clean before its 0.0 surfaced at n=5. **n=2 flipped the conclusion; n=5 corrected it.** Lesson: the de-risk gate (does it saturate?) is reliable at n=2, but per-model *ranking* needs ≥5 samples — the catastrophic failures are ~1-in-5 events.\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-06-02--minimax-capability-discrimination--mimo/eval/strict-validation/synthesis.md:41:- **n=5 per cell** — enough to surface the ~1-in-5 failures and reproduce the gap, but MiMo's exact failure rate has a wide interval; more samples would tighten it.\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-06-02--minimax-capability-discrimination--mimo/eval/strict-validation/synthesis.md:42:- **Framework limitation surfaced:** the reporter's \"TIE-on-format\" headline is misleading when the correctness gate separates the models. Recommended improvement (P2): when only one model is gate-eligible, report it as the correctness winner rather than a format TIE.\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-06-01--prompt-framework--mimo/eval/results-minimax-high-retry.json:5:  \"per_dispatch_timeout_sec\": 120,\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-06-01--prompt-framework--mimo/eval/results-minimax-high-retry.json:17:      \"dispatch_ok\": true,\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-07-10--prompt-framework--minimax/eval-rig/grader/prompts/system-skeptic.md:27:Default to suspicion. Score generously (high score) ONLY if you can affirmatively verify every claim. If you can't verify a symbol exists, treat it as suspicious — your job is to surface what the primary grader might have missed because it was fluency-tuned to reward plausible-looking output.\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-07-10--prompt-framework--minimax/eval-rig/grader/prompts/system-skeptic.md:31:- Function names that follow naming conventions of real APIs but aren't in the framework's public surface\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-07-10--eval-loop--swe-1-6/scripts/render-variant.cjs:6: * concrete prompt-file that cli-devin can dispatch with --prompt-file.\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-06-01--prompt-framework--mimo/eval/runs/cidi--chunk.json:9:  \"dispatched_at\": \"2026-06-02T05:41:50.368Z\",\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-06-02--minimax-capability-discrimination--mimo/synthesis.md:3:Two complementary real-dispatch runs reach the same verdict. The detailed per-run reports and raw\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-06-02--minimax-capability-discrimination--mimo/synthesis.md:36:- n=3 (capability) and n=5 (strict-validation) per cell. Enough to surface the ~1-in-5 failures and\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-07-10--prompt-framework--minimax/eval-loop/scripts/dispatch-swe16.cjs:3: * scripts/dispatch-swe16.cjs\n.opencode/skills/sk-prompt/prompt-models/benchmarks/2026-07-10--prompt-framework--minimax/eva