 succeeded in 0ms:
    55	### Problem Statement
    56	The application currently has no user authentication, allowing anyone to access all features without identity verification. This creates security vulnerabilities, prevents personalization features from being implemented, and blocks the development of user-specific functionality such as saved preferences, order history, and account management.
    57	
    58	### Purpose
    59	Implement a production-ready email/password authentication system that provides secure user registration, login, and session management while establishing patterns and infrastructure for future authentication enhancements.
    60	
    61	
    62	<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->
    63	---
    64	
    65	<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->
    66	## 3. SCOPE
    67	
    68	### In Scope
    69	- User registration with email and password
    70	- User login with session management
    71	- Password hashing using bcrypt
    72	- JWT token generation and validation
    73	- Input validation with clear error messages
    74	- Protection against common attacks (SQL injection, timing attacks)
    75	- Database schema for user storage
    76	- Auth middleware for protected routes
    77	
    78	### Out of Scope
    79	- Social login (OAuth) - spec/013-oauth-integration
    80	- Password reset functionality - spec/014-password-reset
    81	- Two-factor authentication - future enhancement
    82	- Role-based permissions - spec/015-rbac
    83	- Email verification - requires email service
    84	
    85	### Files to Change
    86	
    87	| File Path | Change Type | Description |
    88	|-----------|-------------|-------------|
    89	| src/auth/register.js | Create | Registration form and API handler |
    90	| src/auth/login.js | Create | Login form and session creation |
    91	| src/auth/logout.js | Create | Session termination |
    92	| src/utils/hash.js | Create | Password hashing utilities |
    93	| src/utils/token.js | Create | JWT generation and validation |
    94	| src/middleware/auth.js | Create | Authentication middleware |
    95	| src/validators/auth.js | Create | Input validation schemas |
    96	| prisma/schema.prisma | Modify | Add User model |
    97	| tests/ | Create | Unit and integration tests |
    98	
    99	
   100	<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->
   101	---
   102	
   103	<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->
   104	## 4. REQUIREMENTS
   105	
   106	### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)
   107	
   108	| ID | Requirement |
   109	|----|-------------|
   110	| REQ-001 | Users can register with email/password |
   111	| REQ-002 | Users can log in with valid credentials |
   112	| REQ-003 | Passwords are hashed before storage |
   113	| REQ-004 | Input validation prevents malformed data |
   114	| REQ-005 | Protected routes require authentication |
   115	
   116	### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)
   117	
   118	| ID | Requirement |
   119	|----|-------------|
   120	| REQ-006 | Invalid login shows appropriate error |
   121	| REQ-007 | Session persists across page refresh |
   122	| REQ-008 | Duplicate email registration prevented |
   123	| REQ-009 | Users can log out |
   124	
   125	
   126	
   127	> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,
   128	> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.
   129	<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->
   130	---
   131	
   132	<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->
   133	## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA
   134	
   135	- **SC-001**: User can complete full registration and login flow in under 30 seconds
   136	- **SC-002**: Authentication state persists correctly across browser refresh
   137	- **SC-003**: All security checklist items pass verification
   138	- **SC-004**: Test coverage > 80% for auth modules
   139	
   140	
   141	<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->
   142	---
   143	
   144	<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->
   145	## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES
   146	
   147	| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |
   148	|------|------|--------|------------|
   149	| Dependency | bcrypt library | Cannot hash passwords | Use native crypto as fallback |
   150	| Dependency | jsonwebtoken | Cannot generate sessions | Session-based auth fallback |
   151	| Dependency | Database connection | Cannot store users | Validate DB connection at startup |
   152	| Risk | Token security | Session hijacking | HttpOnly cookies in Phase 2 |
