   107	## 4. REQUIREMENTS
   108	
   109	### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)
   110	
   111	| ID | Requirement |
   112	|----|-------------|
   113	| REQ-001 | Users can register with email/password |
   114	| REQ-002 | Users can log in with valid credentials |
   115	| REQ-003 | Passwords are hashed before storage |
   116	| REQ-004 | Input validation prevents malformed data |
   117	| REQ-005 | Protected routes require authentication |
   118	| REQ-006 | Security review completed |
   119	
   120	### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)
   121	
   122	| ID | Requirement |
   123	|----|-------------|
   124	| REQ-007 | Invalid login shows appropriate error |
   125	| REQ-008 | Session persists across page refresh |
   126	| REQ-009 | Duplicate email registration prevented |
   127	| REQ-010 | Users can log out |
   128	| REQ-011 | Compliance documentation complete |
   129	
   130	
   131	
   132	> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,
   133	> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.
   134	<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->
