   136	
   137	<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->
   138	## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA
   139	
   140	- **SC-001**: User can complete full registration and login flow in under 30 seconds
   141	- **SC-002**: Authentication state persists correctly across browser refresh
   142	- **SC-003**: All security checklist items pass verification
   143	- **SC-004**: Test coverage > 80% for auth modules
   144	- **SC-005**: All approval gates passed
   145	
   146	
   147	<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->
   148	---
   149	
   150	<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->
   151	## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES
   152	
   153	| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |
   154	|------|------|--------|------------|
   155	| Dependency | bcrypt library | Cannot hash passwords | Use native crypto as fallback |
   156	| Dependency | jsonwebtoken | Cannot generate sessions | Session-based auth fallback |
   157	| Dependency | Database connection | Cannot store users | Validate DB connection at startup |
   158	| Dependency | Security team availability | Blocks launch approval | Schedule review early |
   159	| Risk | Token security | Session hijacking | HttpOnly cookies in Phase 2 |
   160	| Risk | Timing attacks | Email enumeration | Constant-time comparison |
   161	
   162	
   163	<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->
   164	---
   165	
   166	<!-- ANCHOR:nfr -->
   167	## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
   168	
   169	### Performance
   170	- **NFR-P01**: Login response time < 500ms (including bcrypt verification)
   171	- **NFR-P02**: Registration response time < 1000ms (including hash generation)
   172	- **NFR-P03**: Token validation < 10ms per request
   173	
   174	### Security
   175	- **NFR-S01**: Passwords hashed with bcrypt (cost factor 10+)
   176	- **NFR-S02**: No sensitive data in error messages (no credential enumeration)
   177	- **NFR-S03**: Input sanitized before database operations
   178	- **NFR-S04**: JWT secrets stored in environment variables only
   179	- **NFR-S05**: OWASP Top 10 authentication items addressed
