   401	
   402	**Exceptions (no spec needed):**
   403	- ❌ Pure exploration/reading (no file modifications)
   404	- ❌ Single typo fixes (<5 characters in one file)
   405	- ❌ Whitespace-only changes
   406	- ❌ Auto-generated file updates (package-lock.json)
   407	
   408	---
   409	
   410	## 13. SKIP OPTION (OPTION D) USAGE
   411	
   412	### When Appropriate ✅
   413	
   414	- Quick code exploration without implementation
   415	- Testing a concept or approach
   416	- Reading/analyzing existing code only
   417	- Prototyping that will be discarded
   418	
   419	### When NOT Appropriate ❌
   420	
   421	- Any actual implementation
   422	- Bug fixes (even small ones)
   423	- Feature work
   424	- Refactoring
   425	- Configuration changes
   426	- Documentation updates
   427	
   428	### Technical Debt Warning
   429	
   430	Skipping documentation:
   431	- Makes future debugging harder
   432	- Loses implementation decisions
   433	- Breaks team handoffs
   434	- Creates incomplete change history
   435	
   436	**Use sparingly.** When in doubt, create spec folder (even minimal Level 1).
   437	
   438	---
   439	
   440	## 14. TEMPLATE ADAPTATION CHECKLIST (PROGRESSIVE ENHANCEMENT)
   441	
   442	Before presenting documentation to user:
   443	
   444	- [ ] All REQUIRED templates for level copied from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/`:
   445	  - [ ] Level 1: spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md + implementation-summary.md
   446	  - [ ] Level 2: Level 1 + acceptance-criteria.md
   447	  - [ ] Level 3: Level 2 + decision-record.md
   448	- [ ] Optional templates copied if needed (Level 3 only)
   449	- [ ] All placeholders replaced (`<PLACEHOLDER>`, `<NEEDS_CLARIFICATION: ...>`)
   450	- [ ] All sample content removed (`<!-- SAMPLE CONTENT -->`)
   451	- [ ] Template footer deleted
   452	- [ ] Metadata block filled correctly
   453	- [ ] All sections filled with actual content (or marked "N/A")
   454	- [ ] Cross-references to sibling documents working
   455	- [ ] Numbering and emojis preserved
   456	- [ ] Structure matches template
   457	- [ ] Descriptive filenames used (for decision records)
   458	
   459	**If ANY unchecked → Fix before user presentation**
   460	**If required template missing → Cannot claim completion**
   461	
   462	---
   463	
   464	## 15. CONTEXT SAVE & HANDOVER
   465	
   466	### Context Save
   467	
   468	**Manual triggers (OpenCode):**
   469	- Command: `/speckit:save`
   470	- Keywords: "save context", "save conversation", "save this"
   471	
   472	**Note:** OpenCode does not support automatic interval-based saves (hooks are event-triggered via plugins, not time-interval).
   473	
   474	**MANDATORY:** Use generate-context.js for memory save:
   475	```
   476	node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json specs/###-folder/
   477	```
   478	
   479	Use `generate-context.js` for routine metadata and index saves. Quick direct edits are allowed only for `_memory.continuity` YAML frontmatter blocks in `implementation-summary.md`.
   480	
   481	> **Recovery Integration:** Packet recovery is canonical-first. Start from `handover.md`, then `_memory.continuity` in `implementation-summary.md`, then the rest of the packet docs before widening with a ripgrep sweep over the specs tree.
   482	
   483	**Phased Resume**: When the target folder has child phases, first resolve
   484	whether you need the coordination root or an active child.
   485	Load/save memory in the child packet by default.
   486	Only load root memory when updating coordination snapshots.
   487	
   488	**Phase-Parent Resume Ladder**: When the resume target is a phase parent (folder has `[0-9]{3}-name/` children with `spec.md` or `description.json`), `/speckit:resume` honors the pointer first:
   489	
   490	1. Read the pointer, from the telemetry store first and then from `derived.last_active_child_id` in the parent's `graph-metadata.json`. When it names an existing child packet inside the parent, recurse into that child at any age, report the child and its `derived.last_active_at`, and apply the child's normal handover → `_memory.continuity` → spec docs ladder. Confirm mode asks first when the pointer is older than 24 hours.
   491	2. If the pointer is null, missing, malformed, points outside the parent, or names a child that no longer exists, fall back to listing children with statuses (sourced from each child's `graph-metadata.json` `derived.status`) and let the user pick.
   492	3. `--no-redirect` flag bypasses the pointer step entirely and shows the parent's spec.md plus child list.
   493	
   494	The pointer is maintained automatically by the generator: a save into a child points every phase-parent ancestor one level down toward it. A save aimed at a phase parent moves the pointers only when a `--full-auto` save routes its continuity into a leaf, and otherwise moves none. A track root keeps its pointer in the telemetry store only. Atomic write via temp+rename. No `_memory.continuity` block exists at a phase parent (per the lean trio policy — parents have no `implementation-summary.md`).
   495	
   496	**Save location:**
   497	- Primary: the active packet's canonical continuity surfaces
   498	- Core continuity block: `_memory.continuity` in `implementation-summary.md`
   499	- No workspace-root fallback; direct CLI targets stay inside the selected root spec or phase packet
   500	
   501	### Session Continuity Save
   502	
   503	**Command:** `/speckit:save`
   504	
   505	**Purpose:** Refresh packet continuity before a pause or handoff while keeping `handover.md`, `_memory.continuity`, and the packet docs aligned for the next `/speckit:resume` pass.
   506	
   507	**Use when:**
   508	- Ending a long session
   509	- Context compaction detected
   510	- Handing off to another session
   511	- Before complex multi-step operations
   512	
   513	---
   514	
   515	## 16. PHASE WORKFLOW SHORTCUTS
   516	
   517	### Phase Commands
   518	
   519	| Command | Description |
   520	|---------|-------------|
   521	| `/speckit:plan :with-phases` | Trigger phase decomposition as pre-workflow in plan or complete |
   522	| `create.sh --phase --phases N --phase-names a,b,c <description>` | Create a phase parent and named child phase folders |
   523	| `create.sh --phase --parent <parent> --phases N --phase-names a,b <description>` | Add named child phases to an existing parent spec |
   524	| `validate.sh <parent> --recursive` | Validate parent and all child phase folders |
   525	| `node .../nested-changelog.js <spec-folder> --write` | Write a packet-local root or phase changelog into the parent packet `changelog/` folder |
   526	
   527	### Phase Quick Reference
   528	
   529	**Detection:** Complexity score >= 25 AND level >= 3, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact
   530	
   531	**Scoring dimensions:** Architectural (10) + Files>15 (10) + LOC>800 (10) + Risk>=2 (10) + Extreme scale (10)
   532	
   533	**Suggested phase counts:**
   534	- Score 25-34: 2 phases
   535	- Score 35-44: 3 phases
   536	- Score 45+: 4 phases
   537	
   538	### Phase Folder Pattern
   539	
   540	```
   541	specs/###-parent/
   542	├── spec.md           # Phase Documentation Map
   543	├── changelog/        # Root + phase changelog artifacts
   544	├── 001-phase-one/    # Independent child spec folder
   545	├── 002-phase-two/
   546	└── 003-phase-three/
   547	```
   548	
   549	### Phase vs Version Sub-Folders
   550	
   551	- **Phases:** Parallel decomposition of different work streams
   552	- **Versions:** Sequential iterations of the same work
   553	
   554	**Full documentation:** See [phase-definitions.md](../structure/phase-definitions.md)
   555	
   556	---
   557	
   558	## 17. AGENT CRITICAL RULES (PROGRESSIVE ENHANCEMENT)
   559	
   560	### Absolutely Required
   561	
   562	- **NEVER create documentation from scratch** - Always copy from templates
   563	- **ALWAYS copy from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/`** directory
   564	- **ALWAYS copy ALL REQUIRED templates for chosen level**:
   565	  - Level 1: spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md + implementation-summary.md
   566	  - Level 2: Level 1 + acceptance-criteria.md
   567	  - Level 3: Level 2 + decision-record.md
   568	- **ALWAYS fill ALL placeholders** - No `<PLACEHOLDER>` marker in final docs
   569	- **ALWAYS respond to workflow prompts** - Ask user for A/B/C/D choice
   570	- **ALWAYS get user approval** - Explicit "yes" before file changes
   571	- **Use distributed governance for spec docs** — Any agent writing packet markdown must use the level templates, run `validate.sh --strict`, and route continuity refreshes through `/speckit:save`. Preserve `@deep-research` ownership of `research/research.md` and `@debug` ownership of `debug-delegation.md`.
   572	
   573	### Enforcement
   574	
   575	- **Verify required templates exist** before claiming completion
   576	- **LOC is one scored input** - run `recommend-level.sh` and go higher when your judgment disagrees
   577	- **Enforcement is `validate.sh --strict` plus `check-completion.sh`** - run both before claiming done
   578	
   579	### Applies to ALL
   580	
   581	- Code files (*.js, *.ts, *.py, *.css, *.html)
   582	- Documentation files (*.md, README, docs/)
   583	- Configuration files (*.json, *.yaml, *.toml)
   584	- Knowledge base files (project-specific)
   585	- Template files (.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/*.md)
   586	- Build files (package.json, requirements.txt)
   587	
   588	**No exceptions** (unless user explicitly selects Option D)
   589	
   590	---
   591	
   592	## 18. CHECKLIST VERIFICATION PROTOCOL (LEVEL 2+)
   593	
   594	### When to Use
   595	
   596	Checklist verification is **MANDATORY** for all Level 2+ documentation:
   597	- Level 2: Features requiring QA validation (100-499 LOC guidance)
   598	- Level 3: Complex/architectural work (>=500 LOC guidance)
   599	- Level 3+: Complex governance/multi-agent work (high complexity/risk)
   600	
   601	The verification region of `tasks.md` is an **ACTIVE VERIFICATION TOOL**, not passive documentation.
   602	
   603	### Verification Process
   604	
   605	```
   606	CHECKLIST AS VERIFICATION TOOL (Level 2+):
   607	1. LOAD the tasks.md verification region at completion phase
   608	2. VERIFY each item systematically (P0 first, then P1, then P2)
   609	3. MARK items [x] with evidence (links, test results, etc.)
   610	4. BLOCK completion until all P0/P1 items verified
   611	5. DOCUMENT any deferred P2 items with reason
   612	```
   613	
   614	### Priority Levels
   615	
   616	| Priority | Meaning | Completion Gate |
   617	|----------|---------|-----------------|
   618	| **P0** | Blocker | MUST pass - work is incomplete without this |
   619	| **P1** | Required | MUST pass - required for production readiness |
   620	| **P2** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |
   621	
   622	### How to Verify Items
   623	
   624	For each checklist item:
   625	
   626	1. **Perform the check** (run test, inspect code, verify behavior)
   627	2. **Mark with [x]** when verified
   628	3. **Add evidence** (link, test output, screenshot reference)
   629	4. **Add timestamp** for audit trail
   630	
   631	### Example: Properly Verified Checklist
   632	
   633	```markdown
   634	## Verification Checklist
   635	
   636	### P0 - Blockers (MUST pass)
   637	- [x] Core functionality works as specified
   638	  - Evidence: Manual test passed - modal opens/closes correctly
   639	  - Verified: 2025-12-01 14:30
   640	- [x] No console errors in browser
   641	  - Evidence: DevTools console clean on Chrome/Firefox/Safari
   642	  - Verified: 2025-12-01 14:32
   643	
   644	### P1 - Required (MUST pass for production)
   645	- [x] Responsive design verified (mobile/tablet/desktop)
   646	  - Evidence: Tested at 375px, 768px, 1440px breakpoints
   647	  - Verified: 2025-12-01 14:35
   648	- [x] Accessibility: keyboard navigation works
   649	  - Evidence: Tab/Enter/Escape all functional
   650	  - Verified: 2025-12-01 14:38
   651	
   652	### P2 - Optional (can defer)
   653	- [ ] Performance optimization for large datasets
   654	  - Deferred: Not needed for MVP, tracked in issue #123
   655	- [x] Animation smoothness verified
   656	  - Evidence: 60fps confirmed in Performance tab
   657	  - Verified: 2025-12-01 14:40
   658	```
   659	
   660	### AI Agent Rules
   661	
   662	- **NEVER claim completion without running checklist verification**
   663	- **ALWAYS load the tasks.md verification region before stating work is done**
   664	- **ALWAYS mark items with evidence, not only [x]**
   665	- **ALWAYS complete all P0/P1 before claiming done**
   666	- **ALWAYS document why P2 items are deferred (if applicable)**
   667	
   668	---
   669	
   670	## 19. CORE PRINCIPLE
   671	
   672	**Every file change deserves documentation.**
   673	
   674	Future you will thank present you for creating that spec folder.
   675	
   676	When in doubt:
   677	- Document more rather than less
   678	- Choose higher level over lower
   679	- Create spec folder over skipping
   680	- Ask user rather than guessing
   681	
   682	**Cost of creating spec << Cost of reconstructing lost context later**
   683	
   684	---
   685	
