    12	---
    13	
    14	# SpecKit Template Migration Guide
    15	<!-- Lives beside spec-kit-docs.json under templates/ (not references/) because it co-locates with the manifest it documents. -->
    16	
    17	Private maintainer notes for template marker and frontmatter compatibility.
    18	
    19	Use this guide when maintaining manifest compatibility with legacy packets, marker formats, and current-version write policy.
    20	
    21	---
    22	
    23	## 1. LEGACY MARKER SUPPORT
    24	
    25	Legacy markers such as `<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.1 -->` remain supported indefinitely.
    26	Readers should parse the template basename and version when present, but they must not reject historical packets only because the marker predates v2.2.
    27	
    28	Writers always emit the current manifest-backed marker version from `spec-kit-docs.json.versions`.
    29	
    30	---
    31	
    32	## 2. BROAD DOCUMENT LIST DERIVATION
    33	
    34	When a legacy packet does not have manifest-aware metadata, derive its document list from files on disk:
    35	
    36	- Always include existing core docs: `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `implementation-summary.md`.
    37	- Include add-on docs when present: `decision-record.md` and `resource-map.md`.
    38	- Include command-owned docs only when present: `handover.md`, `debug-delegation.md`, and `research/research.md`.
    39	- For phase parents, prefer the lean trio: `spec.md`, `description.json`, and `graph-metadata.json`.
    40	
    41	The derived list is read-only compatibility data. Do not rewrite old packets only to normalize marker style.
    42	
    43	---
    44	
    45	## 3. SUNSET POLICY
    46	
    47	There is no planned sunset date for v2.1 marker parsing.
    48	The migration policy is indefinite read support plus current-version writes.
    49	
    50	---
    51	
    52	## 4. NEVER INVENT PROVENANCE
    53	
    54	A tool writes a template-source marker only when the document's anchors exactly equal the anchor set the template renders for the packet's level. A document that does not match keeps no marker, and no marker or comment is ever added to record unknown provenance.
    55	
    56	`check-template-staleness.sh --auto-upgrade` and `quality-audit.sh --fix` were removed, and `upgrade-legacy.mjs` is the repair path.
    57	
    58	---
    59	
    60	## 5. EXTENSION PROCESS LINK
    61	
    62	For new document types, follow `EXTENSION-GUIDE.md` and add both the manifest document entry and a per-document `sectionGates` profile.

