     9	version: 1.0.0.0
    10	---
    11	
    12	# Templates
    13	
    14	---
    15	
    16	## 1. OVERVIEW
    17	
    18	`templates/` contains the markdown templates and manifest data used by the Spec Kit packet scaffolder and validator. It is a content folder rather than a runtime package, but it still has a strict structure because scripts read its files directly.
    19	
    20	Current state:
    21	
    22	- `spec-kit-docs.json` maps public Levels to required docs, add-on docs, lazy docs and section gates.
    23	- `core/`, `addons/` and `packet-types/` `*.md.tmpl` files contain gated markdown blocks rendered by the inline-gate renderer.
    24	- `examples/` stores rendered reference packets for each supported Level.
    25	
    26	---
    27	
    28	## 2. ARCHITECTURE
    29	
    30	```text
    31	╭────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
    32	│                         TEMPLATES                          │
    33	╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
    34	
    35	┌──────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐
    36	│ create.sh        │ ───▶ │ manifest JSON    │
    37	│ packet scaffold  │      │ level contracts  │
    38	└──────────────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘
    39	                                    │
    40	                                    ▼
    41	┌──────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐
    42	│ renderer script  │ ───▶ │ *.md.tmpl        │
    43	│ IF-gate pruning  │      │ packet docs      │
    44	└────────┬─────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘
    45	         │                         │
    46	         ▼                         ▼
    47	┌──────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐
    48	│ output packet    │      │ validate.sh      │
    49	│ specs/...        │ ◀─── │ same contract    │
    50	└──────────────────┘      └──────────────────┘
    51	
    52	Dependency direction:
    53	scripts read templates and manifest data
    54	templates do not call scripts or import runtime modules
    55	```
    56	
    57	---
    58	
    59	## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY
    60	
    61	```text
    62	templates/
    63	├── core/                  │ The required documents every packet carries
    64	├── addons/                │ Optional and on-demand documents
    65	├── packet-types/          │ Templates for special packet shapes
    66	├── spec-kit-docs.json     │ The level contract
    67	├── CONTRACT.md            │ Maintainer guide for the contract
    68	├── examples/              │ Pre-rendered reference packets
    69	├── changelog/             │ Template change records
    70	├── stress-test/           │ Deep-review grading materials
    71	└── scratch/               │ Local debug space, gitignored
    72	```
    73	
    74	Allowed dependency direction:
    75	
    76	```text
    77	runtime/cli/spec/create.sh → templates/spec-kit-docs.json
    78	runtime/cli/templates/inline-gate-renderer.* → templates/{core,addons,packet-types}/*.md.tmpl
    79	runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh → the level contract at templates/spec-kit-docs.json
    80	docs → examples and maintainer guides
    81	```
    82	
    83	Disallowed dependency direction:
    84	
    85	```text
    86	templates/ → generated spec packets
    87	templates/ → runtime engine modules
    88	examples/ → scaffolder input
    89	```
    90	
    91	---
    92	
    93	## 4. DIRECTORY TREE
    94	
    95	```text
    96	templates/
    97	├── README.md
    98	├── spec-kit-docs.json
    99	├── core/
   100	│   ├── spec.md.tmpl
   101	│   ├── plan.md.tmpl
   102	│   ├── tasks.md.tmpl
   103	│   └── implementation-summary.md.tmpl
   104	├── addons/
   105	│   ├── acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl
   106	│   ├── decision-record.md.tmpl
   107	│   ├── handover.md.tmpl
   108	│   ├── debug-delegation.md.tmpl
   109	│   ├── goal.md.tmpl
   110	│   ├── research.md.tmpl
   111	│   ├── resource-map.md.tmpl
   112	│   ├── before-after.md.tmpl
   113	│   ├── timeline.md.tmpl
   114	│   └── roadmap.md.tmpl
   115	├── packet-types/
   116	│   ├── phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl
   117	│   ├── research.spec.md.tmpl
   118	│   ├── review-report.md.tmpl
   119	│   └── review.spec.md.tmpl
   120	├── examples/
   121	│   ├── level-1/
   122	│   ├── level-2/
   123	│   ├── level-3/
   124	│   └── level-3+/
   125	├── changelog/                  # Packet-local changelog templates, versioned by their own v1.0 markers and outside the manifest
   126	└── scratch/
   127	```
   128	
   129	---
   130	
   131	## 5. KEY FILES
   132	
   133	| File                                      | Responsibility                                                                   |
   134	| ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
   135	| `spec-kit-docs.json`             | Defines Level contracts, document registry, template versions and section gates. |
   136	| `core/spec.md.tmpl`                   | Renders feature specification documents.                                         |
   137	| `packet-types/review.spec.md.tmpl`            | Renders review-record specifications for the `review` packet type.               |
   138	| `packet-types/review-report.md.tmpl`          | Renders the nine-section review report for a hand-authored `review` packet.      |
   139	| `packet-types/research.spec.md.tmpl`          | Renders research-record specifications for the `research` packet type.           |
   140	| `core/plan.md.tmpl`                   | Renders implementation plan documents.                                           |
   141	| `core/tasks.md.tmpl`                  | Renders task breakdown documents.                                                |
   142	| `core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl` | Renders delivery summaries and continuity anchors.                               |
   143	| `addons/acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl`    | Renders the closure-gating acceptance criteria for Levels 2, 3 and 3+.           |
   144	| `addons/decision-record.md.tmpl`        | Renders architecture decision records.                                           |
   145	| `addons/handover.md.tmpl`               | Renders handover documents for memory-save workflows.                            |
   146	| `addons/resource-map.md.tmpl`           | Renders optional path ledgers for larger packets.                                |
   147	| `addons/goal.md.tmpl`                   | Renders the durable directive an operator sets as the session objective.        |
   148	| `EXTENSION-GUIDE.md`                      | Explains how maintainers add a new document type.                                |
   149	| `examples/`                               | Shows rendered output for Levels 1, 2, 3 and 3+. Phase-parent scaffolding is defined by the manifest template contract. |
   150	
   151	---
   152	
   153	## 6. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW
   154	
   155	| Boundary  | Rule                                                                                                                                                 |
   156	| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
   157	| Imports   | Scripts read this folder as data. Template files do not import code.                                                                                 |
   158	| Exports   | Rendered packet docs are written into `specs/` by `create.sh`, not by this folder directly.                                                          |
   159	| Ownership | Template content, Level contracts and rendered examples belong here. Runtime validation logic belongs in `runtime/cli/` and `runtime/lib/templates/`. |
   160	
   161	Render flow:
   162	
   163	```text
   164	╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮
   165	│ create.sh receives Level and target path │
   166	╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯
   167	                   │
   168	                   ▼
   169	┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
   170	│ resolver reads spec-kit-docs.json        │
   171	└──────────────────────────────────────────┘
   172	                   │
   173	                   ▼
   174	┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
   175	│ renderer applies IF gates to .md.tmpl    │
   176	└──────────────────────────────────────────┘
   177	                   │
   178	                   ▼
   179	┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
   180	│ scaffold writes rendered docs to specs/  │
   181	└──────────────────────────────────────────┘
   182	                   │
   183	                   ▼
   184	╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮
   185	│ validate.sh checks the same contract     │
   186	╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯
   187	```
   188	
   189	---
   190	
   191	## 7. ENTRYPOINTS
   192	
   193	| Entrypoint                                  | Type              | Purpose                                                  |
   194	| ------------------------------------------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
   195	| `spec-kit-docs.json`               | Data file         | Primary Level and document contract consumed by scripts. |
   196	| `core/`, `addons/` and `packet-types/` `*.md.tmpl`                        | Template files    | Rendered into packet markdown files.                     |
   197	| `examples/level_*`                          | Reference folders | Show expected rendered output by Level.                  |
   198	| `runtime/cli/spec/create.sh`                    | Script caller     | Reads this folder to scaffold packets.                   |
   199	| `runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh`                  | Script caller     | Reads the same contract to validate packets.             |
   200	| `runtime/cli/templates/inline-gate-renderer.sh` | Script caller     | Renders gated template blocks for a selected Level.      |
   201	
   202	---
   203	
   204	## 8. VALIDATION
   205	
   206	Run from the repository root.
   207	
   208	```bash
   209	bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/example --strict
   210	```
   211	
   212	Expected result for a real spec folder: the validator reads the manifest contract and reports no missing required docs or gated sections.
   213	
   214	For template changes, also run the template and resolver test suite used by the repository.
   215	
   216	---
   217	
   218	## 9. RELATED
   219	
   220	- [Contract Guide](./CONTRACT.md)
   221	- [Extension Guide](./EXTENSION-GUIDE.md)
   222	- [Migration Guide](./MIGRATION.md)
   223	- [System Spec Kit Skill](../SKILL.md)
   224	- [Template Resolver](../runtime/lib/templates/level-contract-resolver.ts)
   225	- [Spec Scaffolder](../runtime/cli/spec/create.sh)
   226	- [Spec Validator](../runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh)

