     8	version: 1.0.0.0
     9	---
    10	
    11	# Template Manifest
    12	
    13	---
    14	
    15	## 1. OVERVIEW
    16	
    17	`templates/` (the `core/`, `addons/` and `packet-types/` folders plus `spec-kit-docs.json`) is private implementation infrastructure for Spec Kit template contracts. It maps public Level values to the document set, lazy document lifecycle and section gates consumed by scaffolding and validation code.
    18	
    19	Public and AI-facing surfaces must keep using Level 1, Level 2, Level 3, Level 3+ and phase-parent wording. Private JSON taxonomy stays inside this directory and implementation code.
    20	
    21	---
    22	
    23	## 2. DIRECTORY TREE
    24	
    25	```text
    26	templates/
    27	├── README.md
    28	├── spec-kit-docs.json        # Private source of truth for Level contracts
    29	├── *.md.tmpl                 # Whole-document markdown templates with gates
    30	├── phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl # Lean phase-parent spec template
    31	├── research.spec.md.tmpl     # Research-record spec template for the research packet type
    32	├── review-report.md.tmpl     # Nine-section review report for a hand-authored review packet
    33	└── review.spec.md.tmpl       # Review-record spec template for the review packet type
    34	```
    35	
    36	---
    37	
    38	## 3. KEY FILES
    39	
    40	| File | Role |
    41	|---|---|
    42	| `spec-kit-docs.json` | Maps public levels to internal contract definitions. |
    43	| `*.md.tmpl` | Provides gated markdown source for rendered packet docs. |
    44	| `addons/acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl` | Provides the closure-gating acceptance criteria document for Levels 2, 3 and 3+. |
    45	| `phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl` | Provides the lean parent spec for phase workflows. |
    46	| `review.spec.md.tmpl` | Provides the review-record spec for the review packet type. |
    47	| `review-report.md.tmpl` | Provides the nine-section report a hand-authored review packet starts from; the deep-review loop writes its own. |
    48	| `research.spec.md.tmpl` | Provides the research-record spec for the research packet type. |
    49	
    50	---
    51	
    52	## 4. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW
    53	
    54	Boundaries:
    55	
    56	- This directory owns template contract data only.
    57	- It must not expose private taxonomy in command help, generated packet files, agent prompts or policy docs.
    58	- Generated docs should use public Level labels only.
    59	
    60	Render flow:
    61	
    62	```text
    63	╭────────────────────╮
    64	│ spec-kit-docs.json │
    65	╰─────────┬──────────╯
    66	          ▼
    67	┌────────────────────┐
    68	│ gated template     │
    69	└─────────┬──────────┘
    70	          ▼
    71	┌────────────────────┐
    72	│ renderer script    │
    73	└─────────┬──────────┘
    74	          ▼
    75	┌────────────────────┐
    76	│ public spec doc    │
    77	└────────────────────┘
    78	```
    79	
    80	---
    81	
    82	## 5. ENTRYPOINTS
    83	
    84	| Entrypoint | Use |
    85	|---|---|
    86	| `runtime/cli/templates/inline-gate-renderer.ts` | Render one gated template for one Level. |
    87	| `runtime/cli/templates/inline-gate-renderer.sh` | Shell wrapper for renderer use from scripts. |
    88	| `spec-kit-docs.json` | Contract source read by scaffold and validation code. |
    89	
    90	---
    91	
    92	## 6. VALIDATION
    93	
    94	Run template and spec validation from the repository root after contract edits:
    95	
    96	```bash
    97	npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run typecheck
    98	bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict
    99	```
   100	
   101	Rendered output should match the intended public Level contract and must not leak private manifest terms.
   102	
   103	---
   104	
   105	## 7. RELATED
   106	
   107	| Document | Role |
   108	|---|---|
   109	| [Templates README](../README.md) | Parent template package overview. |
   110	| [Changelog templates](changelog/README.md) | Packet-local changelog template notes. |

