    50	
    51	This is **Phase 3** of the Make system-spec-kit templates and authoring docs followable by a DeepSeek V4.1 Flash agent swarm specification.
    52	
    53	**Scope Boundary**: Edits land only in the files listed in section 3 under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/`, plus this phase folder and the throwaway track `specs/zz-bench-gate/`, which the smoke test creates and deletes. No other template, example, reference or script changes.
    54	
    55	**Dependencies**:
    56	- The launch preconditions in `../spec.md` section 3 are met and recorded in `../goal.md` section 4.
    57	- Phase 2 is closed. It leaves `templates/core` untouched, so this phase starts from the original hints.
    58	- Phase 1 produced `../001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/scratch/ledger/ledger.jsonl` and `../001-template-drift-census-and-baseline/scratch/baseline/suite-start.txt`.
    59	
    60	**Deliverables**:
    61	- The five templates `core/spec.md.tmpl`, `core/plan.md.tmpl`, `core/tasks.md.tmpl`, `core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl` and `addons/acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl` converted to value tokens and stamped v2.3.
    62	- The lifecycle in the orchestrator function `validatePlaceholders` and in the shell rule `rules/check-placeholders.sh`, built and tested together.
    63	- `runtime/cli/tests/placeholder-token-gate.vitest.ts`, which fails before the change and passes after it.
    64	- Before and after counts of strict validation over every packet under `specs/`.
    65	- Five corrected lines in `references/templates/template-guide.md` and a lifecycle section in `references/validation/validation-rules.md`.
    66	
    67	**Changelog**:
    68	- When this phase closes, refresh the matching file in ../changelog/ using the parent packet number plus this phase folder name.
    69	<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->
    70	
    71	---
    72	
    73	<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->
    74	## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE
    75	
    76	### Problem Statement
    77	Phase 1 measured a fresh Level 2 scaffold at 87 distinct hint strings and 97 occurrences, and strict validation passes it. The validator only flags the `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:` token, and the templates do not use that token for their hints, so nothing tells a weak model, or the validator, that a hint is unfilled. Turning on a blanket error would break every existing packet and every external repo, so the gate has to apply to new docs only.
    78	
    79	### Purpose
    80	A packet scaffolded after this phase cannot reach a non-Draft status with an unfilled hint, and no packet written before it changes its verdict.
    81	<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->
    82	
    83	---
    84	
    85	<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->
    86	## 3. SCOPE
    87	
    88	### In Scope
    89	- Convert every bracketed hint in the five templates to `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: <hint text>]` with a script, and stamp the templates v2.3.
    90	- Add the lifecycle to the orchestrator and to the shell mirror, with the same observable behavior.
    91	- A failing-first vitest file with a mutation check for each implementation.
    92	- Regenerate the scaffold golden snapshot, because it renders these templates.
    93	- Update the template manifest versions so the version parity test keeps passing.
    94	- Fix the five `[PLACEHOLDER]` lines in `template-guide.md` and describe the lifecycle in `validation-rules.md`.
    95	- A scaffold smoke test in the throwaway track `specs/zz-bench-gate/`.
    96	- Before and after strict validation over every packet under `specs/`.
    97	
    98	### Out of Scope
    99	- Any change to a doc without the v2.3 stamp. Decision D-b keeps their verdict fixed.
   100	- The other addon and packet-type templates, including `goal.md.tmpl` and `decision-record.md.tmpl`. They keep their v2.2 stamps and bare hints.
   101	- Per-section fill guidance. Phase 4 owns it.
   102	- `runtime/cli/spec/check-placeholders.sh`, the post-edit scanner. `plan.md` ADR-003 records two defects in it as operator items.
   103	- `repo-era.mjs` and `upgrade-level.sh`. `plan.md` ADR-005 and ADR-006 record their side effects as operator items.
   104	- `README.md` and `assets/template-mapping.md`, which also say `[PLACEHOLDER]`. Phase 7 owns the README alignment.
   105	- Committing or pushing.
   106	
   107	### Files to Change
   108	
   109	All paths are under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/` unless they start with `specs/`.
   110	
   111	| File Path | Change Type | Description |
   112	|-----------|-------------|-------------|
   113	| `templates/core/spec.md.tmpl` | Modify | Hints become tokens, 3 stamp lines become v2.3 |
   114	| `templates/core/plan.md.tmpl` | Modify | Same, 1 stamp line |
   115	| `templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl` | Modify | Same, 1 stamp line |
