   132	<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->
   133	## 4. REQUIREMENTS
   134	
   135	### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)
   285	### Anchor crossings to repair
   286	
   287	The command below prints one line per crossing. Run it on every `.tmpl` under `templates` before and after the edit.
   288	
   289	```bash
   290	for f in $(find .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates -name '*.tmpl' | sort); do
   291	  awk 'BEGIN{d=0} /<!-- IF /{d++} /<!-- \/IF -->/{d--} /<!-- ANCHOR:/{match($0,/ANCHOR:[a-z0-9-]+/); a[substr($0,RSTART+7,RLENGTH-7)]=d} /<!-- \/ANCHOR:/{match($0,/ANCHOR:[a-z0-9-]+/); n=substr($0,RSTART+7,RLENGTH-7); if (a[n]!=d) print FILENAME":"NR": anchor "n" opens at "a[n]" closes at "d}' "$f"
   292	done
   293	```
   294	
   295	Observed on the current tree: four lines for `core/spec.md.tmpl` (`nfr`, `edge-cases` and `questions` twice) and two lines for `addons/research.md.tmpl` (`core-architecture`, `changelog-updates`). The third research crossing, `integration-patterns`, sits at one depth and is not reported by the command, and R3 repairs it by inspection. The seven repairs are four in `core/spec.md.tmpl` and three in `addons/research.md.tmpl`.
   296	
   297	Phase 003 runs before this phase and converts every bare hint in `core/spec.md.tmpl` to a value token. T001 writes the token count to `scratch/baseline/locator-form.txt`. A count above `0` means the tree is post-003 and every repair below quotes the post-003 form. A count of `0` means phase 003 is not closed and the repair quotes the pre-token form. An anchor marker holds no hint, so its form is the same on both trees. `addons/research.md.tmpl` is outside the five templates phase 003 converts, so its repairs have one form on both trees.
   298	
   299	Each repair that quotes template text is written as a diff. A line that starts with `-` is removed and a line that starts with `+` is added. The leading `-` or `+` is not part of the template text. A quoted marker is written this way so that it does not read as an anchor of this plan.
   300	
   301	**Fix S1, `nfr`.** The Level 2 anchor marks the Level 2 heading only, because the section body is shared with Level 3 and a pair that spans it would close inside a deeper gate. First insert the closing marker below the Level 2 heading. Remove the two lines and add the three lines:
   302	
   303	```diff
   304	-<!-- ANCHOR:nfr -->
   305	-## L2: NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
   306	+<!-- ANCHOR:nfr -->
   307	+## L2: NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
   308	+<!-- /ANCHOR:nfr -->
   309	```
   310	
   311	Then remove the closing marker that sits after the Level 2-only bullet. Post-003 form, the expected tree:
   312	
   313	```diff
   314	-- **NFR-R02**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Error rate - e.g., <1%]
   315	-<!-- /ANCHOR:nfr -->
   316	-<!-- /IF -->
   317	-<!-- /IF -->
   318	+- **NFR-R02**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Error rate - e.g., <1%]
   319	+<!-- /IF -->
   320	+<!-- /IF -->
   321	```
   322	
   323	Pre-token form, used only when T001 recorded `TOKEN=0`:
   324	
   325	```diff
   326	-- **NFR-R02**: [Error rate - e.g., <1%]
   327	-<!-- /ANCHOR:nfr -->
   328	-<!-- /IF -->
   329	-<!-- /IF -->
   330	+- **NFR-R02**: [Error rate - e.g., <1%]
   331	+<!-- /IF -->
   332	+<!-- /IF -->
   333	```
   334	
   335	**Fix S2, `edge-cases`.** Do the same for the Level 2 anchor, and restore the missing close after the Level 2-only bullet so Level 3 keeps the State Transitions block. First insert the closing marker below the Level 2 heading:
   336	
   337	```diff
   338	-<!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->
   339	-## L2: EDGE CASES
   340	+<!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->
   341	+## L2: EDGE CASES
   342	+<!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->
   343	```
   344	
   345	Then replace the error and transition block. Post-003 form, the expected tree:
   346	
   347	```diff
   348	-### Error Scenarios
   349	-- External service failure: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback behavior]
   350	-<!-- IF level:2,3 -->
   351	-- Network timeout: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Retry strategy]
   352	-<!-- IF level:2 -->
   353	-- Concurrent access: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conflict resolution]
   354	-
   355	-### State Transitions
   356	-- Partial completion: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Recovery behavior]
   357	-- Session expiry: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User experience]
   358	-<!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->
   359	-<!-- /IF -->
   360	-<!-- /IF -->
   361	+### Error Scenarios
   362	+- External service failure: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback behavior]
   363	+<!-- IF level:2,3 -->
   364	+- Network timeout: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Retry strategy]
   365	+<!-- /IF -->
   366	+<!-- IF level:2 -->
   367	+- Concurrent access: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conflict resolution]
   368	+<!-- /IF -->
   369	+
   370	+### State Transitions
   371	+- Partial completion: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Recovery behavior]
   372	+- Session expiry: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User experience]
   373	```
   374	
   375	Pre-token form, used only when T001 recorded `TOKEN=0`:
   376	
   377	```diff
   378	-### Error Scenarios
   379	-- External service failure: [Fallback behavior]
   380	-<!-- IF level:2,3 -->
