   565	  - Level 1: spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md + implementation-summary.md
   566	  - Level 2: Level 1 + acceptance-criteria.md
   567	  - Level 3: Level 2 + decision-record.md
   568	- **ALWAYS fill ALL placeholders** - No `<PLACEHOLDER>` marker in final docs
   569	- **ALWAYS respond to workflow prompts** - Ask user for A/B/C/D choice
   570	- **ALWAYS get user approval** - Explicit "yes" before file changes
   571	- **Use distributed governance for spec docs** — Any agent writing packet markdown must use the level templates, run `validate.sh --strict`, and route continuity refreshes through `/speckit:save`. Preserve `@deep-research` ownership of `research/research.md` and `@debug` ownership of `debug-delegation.md`.
   572	
   573	### Enforcement
   574	
   575	- **Verify required templates exist** before claiming completion
   576	- **LOC is one scored input** - run `recommend-level.sh` and go higher when your judgment disagrees
   577	- **Enforcement is `validate.sh --strict` plus `check-completion.sh`** - run both before claiming done
   578	
   579	### Applies to ALL
   580	
   581	- Code files (*.js, *.ts, *.py, *.css, *.html)
   582	- Documentation files (*.md, README, docs/)
   583	- Configuration files (*.json, *.yaml, *.toml)
