.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/scripts/README.md:23:- `run-tests-sharded.mjs` splits the suite because a single reused worker eventually spins on a CPU-bound rehash storm and never returns. The module it stops at is innocent, and so are the ones after it: the cost belongs to the accumulated process. Shards run one at a time on purpose; running them together contends for the same temporary directories and databases and produces failures that belong to the harness rather than the code.
