    18	---
    19	
    20	## 1. OVERVIEW
    21	
    22	### Template Architecture: Manifest-Backed Level Contracts
    23	
    24	Templates use a manifest-backed model where `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` selects rendered `*.md.tmpl` documents for each Level:
    25	
    26	```
    27	templates/
    28	├── spec-kit-docs.json       # Level contract and document membership
    29	├── spec.md.tmpl             # Requirements and scope
    30	├── plan.md.tmpl             # Technical approach
    31	├── tasks.md.tmpl            # Task breakdown
    32	├── acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl  # Closure criteria (Level 2+)
    33	├── decision-record.md.tmpl  # Architecture decisions
    34	├── implementation-summary.md.tmpl
    35	├── phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl
    36	├── handover.md.tmpl
    37	├── debug-delegation.md.tmpl
    38	├── resource-map.md.tmpl
    39	└── research.md.tmpl          # Optional research notes
    40	```
    41	
    42	### Template Paths - Quick Reference
    43	
    44	| Path | Purpose | When to Use |
    45	|------|---------|-------------|
    46	| `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` | Level contract and document matrix | **ALWAYS use this through `create.sh` for new specs** |
    47	| Level source contract | Source components | Reference only (understanding architecture) |
    48	| Level extension contract | Level additions | Reference only (understanding architecture) |
   315	**All Level 2 content expectations PLUS:**
   316	
   317	**decision-record.md required sections:**
   318	- Context and problem
   319	- Options considered (2-4 typically)
   320	- Decision made
   321	- Rationale
   322	- Consequences and trade-offs
   323	
   324	**Enforcement:** Hard block if `decision-record.md` missing
   325	
   326	### Example Scenarios
   327	
   328	**Good fits for Level 3:**
   329	- Major feature implementation (user dashboard with analytics)
   330	- System redesign (payment flow v2)
   350	- `templates/core/plan.md.tmpl`
   351	- `templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl`
   352	
   353	**Optional:**
   354	- `templates/addons/research.md.tmpl` (render into `research/research.md` when needed)
   355	
   356	### Template Adaptation
   357	
   358	**All Level 2 adaptations PLUS:**
   359	
   360	**decision-record.md:**
   361	1. Document context and problem clearly
   362	2. Present 2-4 viable options (not every possible choice)
   363	3. Fair comparison (pros/cons for each)
   364	4. State clear decision with rationale
   365	5. Document trade-offs honestly
   366	6. Note what was sacrificed for chosen path
   367	7. Use the canonical required filename `decision-record.md` (topic-specific ADR files are supplemental)
   368	8. Remove all sample content
   369	
   370	---
   371	
   372	## 5. LEVEL 3+: EXTENDED DOCUMENTATION (COMPLEXITY SCORE: 80-100)
   373	
   374	### When to Use
   375	
   376	Level 3+ is auto-detected via complexity scoring for highly complex tasks:
   377	- Multi-agent coordination required
   378	- Complex architectural changes with high stakes
   379	- Large-scale migrations or rewrites
   380	- Tasks requiring explicit AI execution protocols
   381	- High coordination needs across multiple systems
   382	
   383	### Required Files (Level 3 + Extended Features)
   384	
   385	- `spec.md` (from Level 3) - With Complexity Assessment section
    80	- Risk flags >= 2: +10
    81	- Extreme scale (Files > 30 OR LOC > 2000): +10
    82	
    83	Phases are recommended when phase score >= 25 (threshold) AND recommended level >= 3.
    84	Score 25-34 → 2 phases; 35-44 → 3 phases; 45+ → 4+ phases.
    85	
    86	A series parent is the one exception. It groups separate small packets that change the same artifact in the same track, and it qualifies without these thresholds. See `../structure/phase-definitions.md` §2.
    87	
    88	---
    89	
    90	## 3. LEVEL MAPPING
    91	
    92	| Score     | Level | Name         | Description                              |
    93	|-----------|-------|--------------|------------------------------------------|
    94	| <25       | 0     | Quick        | Trivial changes, no formal spec needed   |
    95	| 25-44     | 1     | Baseline     | Standard tasks, basic documentation      |
    96	| 45-69     | 2     | Verification | Complex tasks, full verification         |
    97	| 70+       | 3     | Full         | Critical/architectural, comprehensive    |
    98	
    99	**Level 3+ (Extended)** is an override applied on top of Level 3, not a separate score band. Coordination-root packets governing multi-phase efforts should use Level 3+ regardless of complexity score, as they require governance artifacts (phase maps, ADR records) not covered by Level 3.
   100	
   101	### Level 3+ (Extended) Features
   102	
   103	Level 3+ includes everything from Level 3 plus:
   104	- AI Execution Protocol section
   105	- Dependency graph visualization (ASCII/DAG)
   106	- Effort estimation framework
   107	- Extended checklist items (100-150 items)
   108	- Sign-off requirements
    25	Level 1 (Baseline):     spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md + implementation-summary.md
    26	                               ↓
    27	Level 2 (Verification): Level 1 + acceptance-criteria.md
    28	                               ↓
    29	Level 3 (Full):         Level 2 file set + architecture sections; every add-on stays lazy
    30	                               ↓
    31	Level 3+ (Extended):    Level 3 + governance/AI protocol content
    32	```
    33	
    34	### Core Principles
    35	
    36	1. **Never create from scratch** - Always scaffold through `create.sh` or render from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/`
    37	2. **Always adapt to feature** - Templates are starting points, not final documents
    38	3. **Preserve structure** - Preserve section structure and numbering; emojis are optional
    39	4. **Remove placeholders** - Replace ALL `[PLACEHOLDER]` text with actual content
    40	5. **Delete samples** - Remove `<!-- SAMPLE CONTENT -->` blocks before delivery
    41	
    42	### Why Templates Matter
    43	
    44	**Without templates:**
    90	
    91	### Level 1: Baseline Documentation (LOC guidance: <100)
    92	
    93	**Required Templates:** `spec.md` + `plan.md` + `tasks.md` + `implementation-summary.md`
    94	
    95	**Optional completion artifact:** packet-local changelog via `templates/changelog/root.md` when a durable spec-local history is useful
    96	
    97	**Scaffold command:**
    98	```bash
    99	bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh --level 1 --path specs/###-name --name feature-name
   100	```
   101	
   102	**When to use:**
   103	- **All features start here** - this is the minimum documentation
   104	- <100 LOC, as one input to `recommend-level.sh`
   105	- Localized to one component or trivial changes
   295	status: active
   296	created: 2025-11-23
   297	level: 2
   298	estimated_loc: 350
   299	---
   300	```
   301	
   302	### 3. Placeholder Conventions
   303	
   304	**Placeholder types:**
   305	
   306	- `[PLACEHOLDER]` - **MUST** be replaced with actual content
   307	- `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: ...]` - Unknown requirement (flag for user)
   308	- `<!-- SAMPLE CONTENT -->` - Remove before delivery
   309	
   310	**Example before adaptation:**
   355	```
   356	
   357	**Step 2: Fill Metadata Block**
   358	- Set created date (today)
   359	- Set status (usually "draft" or "active")
   360	- Set level (1/2/3/3+)
   361	- Set estimated LOC
   362	- Add other metadata as needed
   363	
   364	**Step 3: Replace ALL Placeholders**
   365	- Search for `[PLACEHOLDER]`
   366	- Replace with actual content
   367	- Verify no placeholders remain
   368	
   369	**Step 4: Review Sample Content**
   370	- Search for `<!-- SAMPLE CONTENT -->`
    38	```
    39	
    40	### Key Points
    41	
    42	- LOC thresholds are **SOFT GUIDANCE** (not enforcement)
    43	- **Enforcement is MANUAL** - verify required templates exist before claiming completion
    44	
    45	---
    63	
    64	## 3. TEMPLATE COPY COMMANDS (PROGRESSIVE)
    65	
    66	### Level 1: Baseline (ALL features start here)
    67	
    68	```bash
    69	bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh --level 1 --path specs/###-name --name feature-name
    70	```
    71	
    72	### Level 2: Verification (complete set)
    73	
   175	- [ ] Determined level (1/2/3/3+) or exempt (typo fix)
   176	- [ ] Created `/specs/[###-short-name]/`
   177	- [ ] Scaffolded ALL REQUIRED templates for chosen level:
   178	  - [ ] Level 1: spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md + implementation-summary.md
   179	  - [ ] Level 2: Level 1 + acceptance-criteria.md
   180	  - [ ] Level 3: Level 2 + decision-record.md
   181	  - [ ] Level 3+: Use full Level 3 file set rendered at Level 3+
   182	- [ ] Rendered template output names are correct
   183	- [ ] Filled ALL template sections with actual content
   184	- [ ] Removed placeholder text and sample sections

