   134	specs/009-notification-system/
   135	├── spec.md        # Feature requirements, acceptance criteria
   160	**Why Level 3**: Significant architectural change affecting multiple systems. Requires documented decision rationale for future reference.
   161	
   162	### Workflow
   163	
   164	**Phase 1: Initiate Planning**
   165	
   166	```bash
   167	User: /spec_kit:plan
   168	AI: Spec folder?
   169	User: B (New)
   170	AI: Feature name?
   171	User: graphql-migration
   172	AI: Documentation level? (Recommended: 3 based on ~800 LOC and architectural impact)
   173	User: 3
   174	```
   175	
   176	**Phase 2: Decision Record Creation**
   177	
   178	Level 3 requires an Architecture Decision Record (ADR):
   179	
   180	```markdown
   181	# ADR-001: GraphQL Migration
   182	
   183	## Status
   184	Approved
   185	
   186	## Context
   187	Current REST API has N+1 query problems causing performance issues.
   188	Mobile clients over-fetch data, increasing bandwidth usage.
   189	
   190	## Decision
   191	Migrate to GraphQL with Apollo Server for the API layer.
   192	
   193	## Consequences
   194	
   195	### Positive
   196	- Reduced over-fetching
   197	- Better developer experience
   198	- Single endpoint simplicity
   199	
   200	### Negative
   201	- Learning curve for team
   202	- Migration period complexity
   203	- Caching strategy changes
   204	```
   205	
   206	### Files Created
   207	
   208	```markdown
   209	specs/010-graphql-migration/
   210	├── spec.md            # Migration scope, success criteria
   211	├── plan.md            # Phased migration approach
   212	├── tasks.md           # Detailed task breakdown
   213	├── acceptance-criteria.md  # the closure gate
   214	├── decision-record.md # ADR documenting rationale
   215	├── implementation-summary.md # Final state, validation evidence
   216	└── scratch/           # Migration scripts, test queries
   217	```
   218	
   219	### Key Takeaways
   220	
   221	| Aspect | Learning |
   222	|--------|----------|
   223	| Decision Record | Level 3 requires decision-record.md (ADR format) |
   224	| Risk Documentation | Consequences section captures trade-offs |
   225	| Rollback Planning | Checklist includes rollback validation |
   226	| Future Reference | ADR serves as historical documentation |
   227	
   228	### Phased Coordination Root (Level 3+)
   229	
   230	Scenario: Large multi-phase effort requiring root coordination.
    12	version: 1.6.0.7
    13	---
    14	
    15	# Auto Mode Contract Reference
    16	
    17	This reference module defines the single canonical `:auto` setup-resolution contract used by every user-invokable `/command:*:auto` surface in spec-kit (`/spec_kit:*`, `/create:*`, `/deep:*`). Each command's §0 cites this contract and supplies only its own per-field Default Resolution Table + `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` field list. The contract semantics, marker grammar, error format, and verification protocol live here.
    18	
    19	---
    20	
   185	
   186	## §8. Out of Scope
   187	
   188	- Commands without paired YAML workflows (`/prompt`, `agent_router`, etc.) — they have no setup-phase surface where the contract applies.
   189	- Skill-internal `:auto` flows (sk-doc, sk-code routing, etc.) — those are skill SKILL.md surfaces, not `/command:*` surfaces.
   190	- YAML workflow internal interaction gates (e.g. mid-loop approval gates) — handled by each YAML's own non-interactivity rules, not this contract.
   191	- Cross-command `:auto` integration (e.g. `/spec_kit:plan:auto` chained into `/spec_kit:implement:auto`) — separate contract concern.
   192	
   193	## §9. PROVENANCE
   194	
   195	Origin: shipped from the deep-review prototype and generalized in the 12-command rollout.
    26	## 2. WHEN TO USE
    27	
    28	- A root spec folder needs a local changelog history beside `implementation-summary.md`
    29	- A phase child folder needs a packet-local changelog entry in the parent `changelog/` folder
    30	- `/spec_kit:complete` or `/spec_kit:implement` finishes work on a root packet or phase child
    31	
    32	---
    33	
